AL INSUFFICIENCY:Adrenal insufficiency is a common complication in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, often requiring steroid treatment.GENE MUTATIONS:Gene mutations related to adrenoleucodistrofia can be studied to aid in diagnosis, although no prevalent mutation has been identified.MORFOLOGICALLY:ALD:Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD) is a genetic disorder that impacts the metabolism of specific fatty acids, resulting in the buildup of very long-chain fatty acids in the body.RIZZO ET AL:Rizzo et al are researchers who demonstrated the effects of oleic acid on fibroblasts from ALD patients in 1986.ACEITE DE LORENZO:Aceite de Lorenzo is a dietary supplement specifically utilized in the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD), a genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. This treatment aims to normalize plasma concentrations of very long-chain fatty acids, particularly focusing on reducing levels of C26:0 in patients with ALD. The formulation of Aceite de Lorenzo combines glycerol trioleate and glycerol trierucate, which work together to achieve this normalization.

While Aceite de Lorenzo has therapeutic benefits, it is important to note that it may also cause side effects, including plaquetopenia (a reduction in platelet count) and a decrease in essential fatty acids. Despite these potential adverse effects, Aceite de Lorenzo remains a significant dietary intervention for managing the symptoms and progression of Adrenoleukodystrophy.GTO:GTO, or glycerol trioleate, is a dietary component utilized in the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). It is recognized as an alternative treatment option that can be continued even if Lorenzo's oil is discontinued due to potential side effects. GTO is notable for its high percentage of oleic acid, which contributes to its therapeutic properties in managing ALD.GTE:GTE, or Glycerol trierucate, is a dietary component characterized by a high percentage of erucic acid. It is utilized in conjunction with GTO for the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). However, it is important to note that GTE treatment may be suspended if patients using Lorenzo's oil experience thrombocytopenia.C26:0:C26:0, also known as hexacosanoic acid, is a very long-chain saturated fatty acid that plays a significant role in the diagnosis of adrenoleucodystrophy (ALD). This fatty acid accumulates in patients suffering from ALD, and efforts are made to reduce its levels through dietary interventions.√ÅCIDO OLEICO:√Åcido Oleico is a monounsaturated fatty acid recognized for its safety in emulsions intended for patients requiring nutritional support. Additionally, it has been utilized in fibroblast cultures to lower levels of C26:0 in patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). This dual application highlights its significance in both nutritional and therapeutic contexts.√ÅCIDO ER√öCICO:√Åcido er√∫cico es un √°cido graso que se encuentra en los l√≠pidos plaquetarios y est√° relacionado con la plaquetopenia en pacientes que utilizan aceite de Lorenzo. Este √°cido graso tambi√©n se encuentra en aceites de colza y mostaza, y es importante destacar que los pacientes con adrenoleucodistrofia (ALD) no pueden metabolizarlo adecuadamente.DIETA RESTRINGIDA:The restricted diet is a treatment approach for ALD that limits saturated very long-chain fatty acids.NIVEL PLASM√ÅTICO:Plasma levels refer to the concentration of fatty acids in the blood, which are monitored in ALD patients.FIBROBLASTOS:ADRENOLEUCOMIELOPAT√çA:La adrenoleucomielopat√≠a es una enfermedad neurol√≥gica que puede no responder al tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo en estados avanzados.TRASPLANTE DE M√âDULA √ìSEA:The "TRASPLANTE DE M√âDULA √ìSEA" refers to a bone marrow transplant procedure that is sometimes utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions, including Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). This procedure may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition to help reduce infection rates during recovery. While bone marrow transplants have been performed in certain cases of ALD, the effectiveness of this treatment remains uncertain, particularly in advanced stages of the disease. However, it is considered a treatment option for patients who exhibit moderate neurological involvement in ALD.PACIENTES ASINTOM√ÅTICOS:Los pacientes asintom√°ticos pueden beneficiarse del tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo, que reduce la frecuencia y severidad del deterioro neurol√≥gico.PACIENTES CON DISFUNCI√ìN ADRENAL:Los pacientes con disfunci√≥n adrenal o neurol√≥gica preexistente pueden no ver mejoras con el tratamiento de aceite de Lorenzo.VALPROATO:Valproato is a medication that has shown neuroprotective capabilities in animal models for adrenoleucodistrofia and has potential antioxidant effects in patients.LOVASTATINA:Lovastatina, also known as lovastatin, is a medication primarily used to reduce cholesterol levels in the body. Its effectiveness can be influenced by food intake. Additionally, lovastatina has therapeutic applications beyond cholesterol management; it can also reduce AGCML levels in patients suffering from adrenoleucodistrofia. The drug functions by inhibiting nitric oxide synthase, contributing to its diverse pharmacological effects.BETA-INTERFER√ìN:Beta-interfer√≥n is an immunosuppressive agent that has been tested for reducing inflammatory responses in brain lesions associated with ALD but has not shown significant clinical improvement.MITOXANTRONE:Mitoxantrone is an immunosuppressive agent that has been trialed for treating ALD-related brain lesions without significant success.INMUNOGLOBULINAS:Immunoglobulins, also known as "inmunoglobulinas," are antibodies produced by the immune system that play a crucial role in identifying and neutralizing pathogens such as bacteria and viruses. They are essential components of the immune response and are found in bodily fluids like chyle. In addition to their protective functions, inmunoglobulinas have been investigated as immunosuppressive agents in the treatment of autoimmune liver disease (ALD) to help reduce inflammation. However, studies have indicated that they have not demonstrated significant clinical improvement in this context. Overall, inmunoglobulinas are vital for immune defense while also being explored for their potential therapeutic applications in certain medical conditions.BACLOFENO:Baclofeno is a medication used to treat spasticity as a complication of adrenoleucodistrofia.VIGABATRINA:Vigabatrina is a drug used to treat seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.FENOBARBITAL:Fenobarbital is a medication that enhances penetration into the nervous system and has a delayed elimination effect, which can lead to drowsiness. It is primarily used to control seizures in patients suffering from adrenoleucodystrophy.GENE X-ALD:Gene X-ALD is a gene related to adrenoleucodistrofia that is being researched for gene therapy applications.MITOCONDRIA:Mitochondria are cellular organelles where lipid Œ≤-oxidation occurs, crucial for energy production during fasting and stress.PEROXISOMAS:Peroxisomas are cellular organelles involved in lipid metabolism, particularly in the context of AGCML in adrenoleucodistrofia.LESIONES CEREBRALES:Lesiones cerebrales are brain lesions that occur in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy, leading to neurological symptoms.TRATAMIENTO ESTEROIDEO:Tratamiento esteroideo refers to steroid treatment that is essential for managing adrenal function in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy.DIETA CONTROLADA:Dieta controlada en √°cidos grasos is a dietary intervention indicated for metabolic disorders affecting lipid oxidation.ESPASTICIDAD:Espasticidad is a condition that can occur as a complication of adrenoleukodystrophy, requiring specific treatment.FUNCION SUPRARRENAL:Funci√≥n suprarrenal refers to adrenal function, which is crucial to monitor in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy for appropriate steroid treatment.ESTUDIOS ADICIONALES:Estudios adicionales are further studies required to better understand and treat adrenoleukodystrophy.Œí-OXIDACI√ìN:La Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n es un proceso metab√≥lico crucial que descompone √°cidos grasos para producir energ√≠a. Este proceso puede verse afectado en ciertos trastornos metab√≥licos, como la adrenoleucodistrofia, donde se altera la capacidad del organismo para oxidar √°cidos grasos de cadena muy larga.S√çNDROME REYE-LIKE:El s√≠ndrome Reye-like es una condici√≥n m√©dica que puede presentarse en trastornos de la Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n de √°cidos grasos de cadena larga, caracterizada por hipoglucemia y afectaci√≥n neurol√≥gica.AGCL:Los √°cidos grasos de cadena larga (AGCL) son un tipo de grasa que puede verse afectada en trastornos metab√≥licos, especialmente en la Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n.AGCM:Los √°cidos grasos de cadena media (AGCM) son un tipo de grasa que se metaboliza de manera diferente y puede ser utilizado en el tratamiento de trastornos de la Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n.HIPOGLOCEMIA:La hipoglucemia es una condici√≥n caracterizada por niveles bajos de glucosa en la sangre, que puede ser un s√≠ntoma de trastornos de la Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n.NEUROPAT√çA:Neuropat√≠a is a disorder that affects the nerves and can be a symptom of metabolic disorders related to Œ≤-oxidation. It is also recognized as a potential complication of metabolic disorders such as Adrenoleukodystrophy, which impacts nerve function.ARRITMIAS CARD√çACAS:Arritmias card√≠acas are heart rhythm disorders that can manifest in patients with various metabolic disorders, including Adrenoleukodystrophy. These cardiac arrhythmias are characterized as alterations in the heart's rhythm and may serve as a symptom of disorders related to the Œ≤-oxidation of fatty acids.TRASTORNOS METAB√ìLICOS:C24:0:C24:0 es un √°cido graso que se utiliza en la ratio para el diagn√≥stico de adrenoleucodistrofia.C22:0:C22:0 es un √°cido graso que se utiliza en la ratio para el diagn√≥stico de adrenoleucodistrofia.TCM:TCM, or Triglycerides of Medium Chain, refers to a type of dietary fat characterized by a chain length of 6 to 12 carbon atoms. These fats are known for their rapid absorption and metabolism in the body, making them beneficial for improving energy absorption and metabolism. TCM is commonly derived from coconut oil and is utilized in various nutritional products aimed at providing energy. Additionally, TCM is significant in dietary treatments, particularly for patients with specific conditions such as adrenoleucodystrophy, where the intake of medium-chain triglycerides may need to be restricted. Furthermore, TCM is used to reduce the intake of omega-6 fatty acids in lipid emulsions, highlighting its role in nutritional management.TCL:TCL is an organization that focuses on dietary modifications and nutritional supplementation, with a particular emphasis on low-fat diets and medium-chain triglycerides (TCM). In the context of nutrition, TCL also refers to Triglycerides of Long Chain, which are dietary fats that require bile salts for absorption and are metabolized differently than TCM. Additionally, TCL is associated with the treatment of nutritional disorders related to Œ≤-oxidation, where long-chain triglycerides play a significant role. Overall, TCL encompasses both the promotion of specific dietary practices and the understanding of different types of triglycerides in nutritional health.MIELINA:La mielina es una sustancia que se acumula an√≥malamente en la adrenoleucodistrofia, afectando la funci√≥n neurol√≥gica.CORTEZA ADRENAL:La corteza adrenal es otra √°rea donde se acumulan √°cidos grasos de cadena muy larga en la adrenoleucodistrofia.ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY:Adrenoleukodystrophy is a genetic disorder that primarily affects lipid metabolism, leading to the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids in the body. This condition has significant impacts on both the nervous system and the adrenal glands, resulting in a range of neurological symptoms. The disorder is characterized by its progressive nature, which can lead to severe complications if not managed appropriately.VAN GEEL BM:Van Geel BM is an author of a study on X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy, focusing on clinical presentation, diagnosis, and therapy.GIR√ìS M:Giros M is an author involved in the protocol for diagnosis, treatment, and follow-up of X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy.MOSER HW:Moser HW is a researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the study and treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy, particularly focusing on dietary management and the clinical aspects of the condition. His work has been influential in advancing the understanding and therapeutic approaches to this rare genetic disorder.TRASTORNOS DE LA Œí-OXIDACI√ìN:Trastornos de la Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n are metabolic disorders that affect the breakdown of fatty acids and are relevant to the discussion of Adrenoleukodystrophy.HIPOGLUCEMIA NO CET√ìSICA:Hipoglucemia no cet√≥sica is a symptom associated with metabolic disorders, including those related to Adrenoleukodystrophy.MIOTOPAT√çA:Miopat√≠a is a condition that can accompany metabolic disorders like Adrenoleukodystrophy, affecting muscle function.AGENTES ANTIINFLAMATORIOS:Agentes antiinflamatorios are medications that have been explored for modifying the inflammatory response in Adrenoleukodystrophy but have shown limited efficacy.√ÅCIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA MUY LARGA:ADRENOMYELONEUROPATHY:Adrenomyeloneuropathy is a related condition that primarily affects the spinal cord and peripheral nerves, often associated with adrenoleukodystrophy.LORENZO'S OIL:Lorenzo's Oil is a dietary therapy used in the treatment of adrenoleukodystrophy, consisting of a mixture of oleic and erucic acids.JOHN HOPKINS MEDICAL JOURNAL:John Hopkins Med J is a medical journal that publishes research and findings related to various medical conditions, including adrenoleukodystrophy.RIZZO WB:Rizzo WB is a researcher known for his work on fatty acid metabolism and its implications in adrenoleukodystrophy.BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION:Bone Marrow Transplantation is a journal dedicated to publishing research on hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and related fields. The term "bone marrow transplantation" refers to a medical procedure that involves administering high doses of chemotherapy followed by the infusion of hematopoietic cells. This procedure is primarily used to treat various conditions, particularly hematological malignancies, where the bone marrow is either replaced or supplemented. Additionally, bone marrow transplantation serves as a treatment option for several genetic disorders, such as adrenoleukodystrophy, with the goal of restoring normal function in the central nervous system.KISHIMOTO Y:Kishimoto Y is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of fatty acid abnormalities in adrenoleukodystrophy.VAN DUYN MA:Van Duyn MA is a researcher involved in studies related to dietary therapies for adrenoleukodystrophy.FATTY ACID ABNORMALITY:QUILOT√ìRAX:QUILOT√ìRAX is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can manifest as a pleural effusion and may lead to symptoms such as dyspnea (difficulty breathing) and cough. Chylothorax can occur spontaneously or as a result of trauma, often linked to surgical procedures or disorders of the lymphatic system. Treatment for QUILOT√ìRAX typically involves dietary modifications, including specific diets aimed at managing fat metabolism, as well as various medical interventions. These interventions may include surgical techniques and interventional radiology, depending on the underlying cause of the condition. Overall, careful management is essential to address the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural cavity and to alleviate associated symptoms.ASCITIS QUILOSA:Ascitis quilosa is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of chyle, a lymphatic fluid, in the abdominal cavity. This condition often arises due to the rupture or obstruction of abdominal lymphatic ducts and is typically observed around the fifth postoperative day when patients have begun an oral diet. Ascitis quilosa can lead to significant nutritional deficiencies and may necessitate dietary modifications or surgical intervention. It is associated with various medical conditions and can cause symptoms such as abdominal distension. Treatment approaches for ascitis quilosa may include conservative management or surgical options, depending on the severity and underlying causes. In summary, ascitis quilosa involves the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the peritoneal cavity, requiring specific medical and dietary management to address the associated complications.M.¬™ NURIA VIRGILI CASAS:M.¬™ Nuria Virgili Casas is a medical professional involved in the study and treatment of nutritional and metabolic disorders.RAFAEL L√ìPEZ URDIALES:Rafael L√≥pez Urdiales is a medical professional contributing to research in clinical nutrition and metabolism.EVA MAR√çA GARC√çA RAIMUNDO:Eva Mar√≠a Garc√≠a Raimundo is a medical professional focused on nutrition and dietetics in clinical settings.M√ìNICA MONTSERRAT GIL DE BERNAB√â:M√≥nica Montserrat Gil de Bernab√© is a medical professional working in the field of nutrition and dietetics.HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI DE BELLVITGE:Hospital Universitari de Bellvitge is a hospital located in Hospitalet de Llobregat, Barcelona, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.GAUCHER DISEASE TYPE III:Gaucher disease type III is a genetic disorder that affects the body's ability to break down certain fats, leading to various health complications.HURLER SYNDROME:Hurler syndrome is a genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme needed to break down glycosaminoglycans, leading to various physical and cognitive impairments.MAROTEAUX-LAMY SYNDROME:Maroteaux-Lamy syndrome is a genetic disorder that affects connective tissue and is characterized by skeletal abnormalities and other systemic issues.SLY SYNDROME:Sly syndrome is a rare genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that leads to the accumulation of certain substances in the body, affecting various organs.MANNOSIDOSIS:Mannosidosis is a genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that breaks down mannosaccharides, leading to various health issues.FUCOSIDOSIS:Fucosidosis is a rare genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that breaks down fucose, leading to a range of symptoms including neurological issues.ASPARTYGLUCOSAMINURIA:Aspartylglucosaminuria is a genetic disorder characterized by the accumulation of aspartylglucosamine, leading to various health complications.X-LINKED ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY:CONDUCTO TOR√ÅCICO:El conducto tor√°cico es un conducto linf√°tico que transporta la linfa desde el sistema linf√°tico al sistema venoso, desembocando en la confluencia de la vena subclavia y la vena yugular interna izquierdas.SISTEMA LINF√ÅTICO:The "SISTEMA LINF√ÅTICO" is a vital system in the body responsible for transporting lymph, a fluid that contains white blood cells and various other components, through lymphatic vessels to the circulatory system. It is a complex network of tissues and organs that plays a crucial role in the body's immune function by helping to eliminate toxins, waste, and other unwanted materials. This system is essential for maintaining overall health and supporting the body's defense mechanisms.CARCINOMATOSIS PERITONEAL:Peritoneal carcinomatosis refers to the spread of cancer to the peritoneum, which can cause ascitis quilosa.SARCOMA DE KAPOSI:Kaposi's sarcoma is a type of cancer that can lead to complications such as ascitis quilosa.AMILOIDOSIS:Amyloidosis is a disease characterized by the accumulation of amyloid proteins in various organs, which can lead to serious health conditions. This condition can result in complications such as ascitis quilosa and is associated with chronic intestinal pseudo-obstruction, affecting multiple organs, including the gastrointestinal system. The buildup of these abnormal proteins can impair the function of the intestines, potentially affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating the use of parenteral nutrition for affected individuals.LINFANGIOLEIOMATOSIS:Lymphangioleiomyomatosis is a rare lung disease that can cause chylothorax and may be associated with ascitic conditions.TROMBOSIS VENA SUBCLAVIA IZQUIERDA:Left subclavian vein thrombosis can lead to complications affecting lymphatic drainage, potentially resulting in ascitis quilosa.BOCIO ENDOTOR√ÅCICO:Endothoracic goiter is a condition that can cause obstruction of lymphatic flow, potentially leading to ascitic conditions.QUILOT√ìRAX CONG√âNITO:TORACOCENTESIS:La toracocentesis es un procedimiento m√©dico utilizado para extraer l√≠quido del espacio pleural, que puede ayudar en el diagn√≥stico del quilot√≥rax.PARACENTESIS:La paracentesis es un procedimiento m√©dico para extraer l√≠quido del abdomen, utilizado en el diagn√≥stico de ascitis quilosa.AN√ÅLISIS MICROBIOL√ìGICO:AN√ÅLISIS MICROBIOL√ìGICO refers to a microbiological analysis procedure that is essential for various medical evaluations. This analysis is particularly important in clinical settings, as it can be necessary to rule out infections in cases such as pleural effusion or ascites. Additionally, microbiological analysis plays a crucial role in the evaluation of enteral nutrition products, ensuring their safety and efficacy for patient use.T√âCNICAS DE IMAGEN:Las t√©cnicas de imagen son m√©todos utilizados para diagnosticar y localizar lesiones en condiciones como el quilot√≥rax.LINFOGRAF√çA:La linfograf√≠a es una t√©cnica de imagen utilizada para evaluar el sistema linf√°tico y puede ser √∫til en el diagn√≥stico de quilot√≥rax.DERRAME PLEURAL:LINFOCITOS T:LINFOCITOS T, or T lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell that play a central role in cell-mediated immunity. They are crucial for the immune response, helping the body to identify and eliminate pathogens and infected cells.LINFOCITOS B:B lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell that produce antibodies and are essential for humoral immunity.QUILOT√ìRAX ASOCIADO A TUMOR:Quilot√≥rax associated with a tumor refers to the condition of lymphatic fluid accumulation in the pleural cavity that is linked to the presence of a tumor, affecting prognosis.TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL√ìGICO:The entity "TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL√ìGICO" refers to pharmacological treatment, which involves the use of medications to manage various medical conditions. Specifically, it includes the administration of drugs such as somatostatin or octreotide, which are utilized to address conditions like quilot√≥rax (chylothorax) and ascitis quilosa (chylous ascites). Additionally, pharmacological treatment may also affect a patient's ability to receive enteral nutrition, indicating that the use of these medications can have implications for nutritional management in patients undergoing such treatments.TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR:"TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR" refers to a management approach that employs non-surgical methods to address medical conditions such as chylothorax and chylous ascites. This treatment strategy emphasizes dietary modifications and medical therapies as initial interventions, prioritizing resolution of the condition without resorting to invasive surgical options.DIETA MODIFICADA:The "DIETA MODIFICADA" refers to a therapeutic dietary approach specifically designed to manage conditions such as quilot√≥rax and ascitis quilosa. This modified diet focuses on reducing the intake of long-chain triglycerides while supplementing with medium-chain triglycerides. The primary goal of the dieta modificada is to address the unique nutritional needs associated with these health conditions, promoting better health outcomes through careful dietary management.TEJIDOS PERIF√âRICOS:Tejidos perif√©ricos refers to peripheral tissues in the body where fatty acids are transported and utilized.ALIMENTARY SUPPLEMENTATION:Nutritional supplementation with TCM is a dietary approach aimed at enhancing energy intake and improving the organoleptic properties of low-fat diets.LIPIDS:LIPIDS are a group of fats that play a crucial role in nutrition and energy supply. They are particularly important in medical settings, such as in patients with prolonged stays in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU), where lipid emulsions serve as a source of energy and essential fatty acids. The evaluation of lipids focuses on their fatty acid composition and stability, especially in nutritional products designed for various dietary needs. In the context of pancreatitis, lipids can be administered intravenously; however, their use is controversial due to potential complications that may arise. Additionally, dietary advice regarding the selection of foods in modified diets often emphasizes the importance of long-chain and medium-chain triglycerides, highlighting the diverse applications and considerations surrounding lipids in both clinical and dietary contexts.ZUMOS DE FRUTAS Y VERDURAS:Fruit and vegetable juices are allowed in the modified diet as part of the beverage group.INFUSIONES:Infusions are permitted beverages in the modified diet.REFRESCOS:Sodas are allowed in the modified diet as part of the beverage group.PASTA ITALIANA SIN HUEVO:Egg-free Italian pasta is permitted in the modified diet.S√âMOLA:Semolina is included in the permitted food items for the modified diet.GALLETAS INTEGRALES SIN GRASA:Whole grain cookies without fat are allowed in the modified diet.PESCADO BLANCO:PESCADO BLANCO refers to white fish, which is permitted in modified diets. It is traditionally recommended due to its lower phosphorus content when compared to blue fish, making it a favorable choice for those needing to manage their phosphorus intake.MOLUSCOS Y CRUST√ÅCEOS:MOLUSCOS Y CRUST√ÅCEOS, which refers to shellfish and crustaceans, are known to be high in purines, which can lead to elevated uric acid levels in the body. However, they are permitted in modified diets, indicating that their consumption can be managed or included under certain dietary guidelines.CLARA DE HUEVO:Egg whites are permitted in the modified diet.MERMELADA:Jam is permitted in the modified diet as part of the sweets and desserts group.HELADOS DE AGUA:Water-based ice creams are permitted in the modified diet.PASTELER√çA CASERA:Homemade pastries are allowed in the modified diet if made with permitted ingredients.MANTECA DE CERDO:Lard is not allowed in the modified diet.CARNES GRASAS:CARNES GRASAS refers to fatty meats that are characterized by their high fat content. These meats should be limited in children's diets to promote better health outcomes, as they can contribute to various health issues. Additionally, CARNES GRASAS are high in purines, which can lead to increased uric acid levels in the body. Due to these health concerns, fatty meats are not permitted in modified diets, emphasizing the need for careful dietary management to ensure overall well-being.GANSO:Goose is not permitted in the modified diet.V√çSCERAS:Organ meats are not permitted in the modified diet.YEMA DE HUEVO:YEMA DE HUEVO, or egg yolk, is characterized by a high phosphorus content, exceeding 30 mg/g. Due to this elevated phosphorus ratio, it is recommended that egg yolk be limited in consumption. Furthermore, in the context of a modified diet, egg yolk is not permitted, indicating that individuals following such a diet should avoid its inclusion.PESCADO AZUL:PESCADO AZUL refers to blue fish, which is generally discouraged in dietary recommendations due to its higher phosphorus content. However, it is noted that some blue fish may have a favorable phosphorus to protein ratio. Despite this, in the context of a modified diet, blue fish is not permitted.PESCADO O MARISCO ENLATADO EN ACEITE:Canned fish or seafood in oil is not permitted in the modified diet.CHOCOLATES:Chocolates are not permitted in the modified diet, as they are discouraged due to their high phosphorus and potassium content.PASTELER√çA EN GENERAL:General pastries are not allowed in the modified diet.REPOSTER√çA CASERA O COMERCIAL:Homemade or commercial pastries containing prohibited ingredients are not allowed in the modified diet.)<|COMPLETE|>ACEITE MCT:El Aceite MCT es un preparado de triglic√©ridos de cadena media utilizado en dietas para proporcionar energ√≠a y nutrientes a pacientes con necesidades especiales.F√çSTULAS DEL CONDUCTO TOR√ÅCICO:Las f√≠stulas del conducto tor√°cico son condiciones m√©dicas que pueden requerir tratamiento nutricional especializado, como la nutrici√≥n enteral o parenteral.ACEITE MCT¬Æ:Aceite MCT¬Æ is a nutritional supplement with a high percentage of medium-chain triglycerides (MCT), used for various dietary needs.LIQUIGEN¬Æ:Liquigen¬Æ is a nutritional supplement that contains a moderate percentage of MCT, designed for specific dietary requirements.MCT DUOCAL¬Æ:MCT Duocal¬Æ is a nutritional product with a significant MCT content, aimed at providing energy and nutrition.MCT M√ÅS ESENCIALES¬Æ:MCT M√ÅS ESENCIALES¬Æ is a clinical nutrition product that contains a high percentage of MCT, used for dietary management.MCT NM¬