specific dietary management.FRESENIUS:Fresenius is a healthcare group that provides products and services for dialysis, hospital, and nutritional care.SHS:OCTREOTIDA:Octreotide is a synthetic analog of somatostatin, primarily utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions, including quilot√≥rax and ascitis quilosa. It is often administered through continuous infusion. In addition to its standalone use, octreotide is also employed in conjunction with dietary treatments to help reduce lymphatic flow, thereby enhancing clinical outcomes for patients.ETILNEFRINA:Etilnefrina is a sympathomimetic drug that reduces lymphatic flow in the thoracic duct by contracting the smooth muscle of its wall.TRATAMIENTO QUIR√öRGICO:The entity "TRATAMIENTO QUIR√öRGICO" refers to surgical treatment options indicated for various medical conditions. Specifically, surgical treatment is recommended for patients suffering from severe pancreatic conditions, especially in cases where complications arise, such as bile duct obstruction or the presence of pseudo cysts. Additionally, surgical intervention is advised for refractory cases of chylothorax and chylous ascites, which involves procedures aimed at repairing injuries to the lymphatic ducts. This comprehensive approach highlights the critical role of surgical treatment in managing complex medical issues.F√çSTULAS LINF√ÅTICAS:Lymphatic fistulas are abnormal connections that can form between lymphatic vessels and other structures, often requiring surgical intervention.FLUJO LINF√ÅTICO:EMBOLIZACI√ìN:Embolization is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat conditions such as quilot√≥rax and lymphatic fistulas, showing high success rates in traumatic cases.F√çSTULAS QUILOSAS:CHYLOUS ASCITES:Chylous ascites is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the abdominal cavity. This condition often necessitates specific diagnosis and management strategies to address the underlying causes and alleviate symptoms.CHYLOTHORAX:Chylothorax is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can arise due to various factors, including trauma or complications from surgical procedures. Management of chylothorax often necessitates specific nutritional support to address the underlying issues associated with the accumulation of this fluid.HEAD & NECK:Head & Neck is a medical journal that publishes research related to surgery and treatment of head and neck conditions, including chylous leakage.EUR J CARDIOTHORACIC SURG:Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg is a journal that publishes articles on surgical techniques and management of thoracic and cardiovascular conditions, including chylothorax.ARCH SURG:Arch Surg is a journal dedicated to the field of surgery, encompassing a wide range of surgical practices and research. It publishes studies that address various aspects of surgical care, including postoperative complications such as chylous ascites, as well as topics related to immunonutrition. Through its contributions, Arch Surg aims to advance the understanding and application of surgical techniques and patient management in the medical community.MAYO CLINIC PROC:Mayo Clinic Proceedings is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews on various medical topics, including pleural liquid characteristics of chylothorax.BRITISH JOURNAL OF COMMUNITY NURSING:The British Journal of Community Nursing (Br J Comun Nurs) is a scholarly journal dedicated to the exploration and discussion of community nursing practices. It focuses on various aspects of community nursing, including the management of nutritional issues related to chyle leaks and chylous effusions. The journal publishes a range of research articles and discussions that contribute to the field of community nursing, emphasizing the importance of effective nutritional management within this context.ALLEN DB:Allen dB is an author who co-authored the collective review on chylous ascites published in Surgery 2000.ORGAN C.H:Organ C.H is an author who contributed to the collective review on chylous ascites published in Surgery 2000.NAIR S.K:Nair S.K is an author who wrote about the aetiology and management of chylothorax in adults in Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg 2007.PETKO M:Petko M is an author who co-authored the article on the aetiology and management of chylothorax in adults in Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg 2007.HAYWARD M.P:Hayward M.P is an author who contributed to the article on the aetiology and management of chylothorax in adults in Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg 2007.SMOKE A:Smoke A is an author who discussed the consensus on management of chyle leaks in Nutr Clin Pract 2008.DE LEGGE MH:De Legge MH is an author who co-authored the article on chyle leaks in Nutr Clin Pract 2008.JOHNSTONE DW:Johnstone DW is an author who wrote about postoperative chylothorax in Chest Surg Clin N Am 2002.MCGRATH EE:McGrath EE is an author who discussed chylothorax in the article published in Respiratory Medicine 2010.ALEXANDRAKIS M.G:Alexandrakis M.G is an author who wrote about pleural effusions in hematologic malignancies in Chest 2004.B√úTIKER V:B√ºtiker V is an author who discussed chylothorax in children in the guidelines published in Chest 1999.KUZDZAL J:Kuzdzal J is an author who wrote about lymphangioleiomyomatosis presenting as a refractory chylothorax in J Cardiovasc Surg 2005.ABLANK CJ:Ablan CJ is an author who reported on postoperative chylous ascites in Arch Surg 1990.LATERRE PF:Laterre PF is an author who discussed chylous ascites in Acta Gastroenterol Belg 2000.LEIBOVITCH I:Leibovitch I is an author who wrote about the diagnosis and management of postoperative chylous ascites in J Urol 2002.MANOLITSAS T.P:Manolitsas T.P is an author who discussed chylous ascites following treatment for gynecologic malignancies in Gynecol Oncol 2002.YOL S:Yol S is an author who reported a rare complication of D3 dissection for 