≠nez Brocca is a researcher focused on nutritional support in specific medical conditions.KELLY:Kelly is a researcher who studied the management of postoperative chylothorax.HUANG:Huang is a researcher who investigated treatment options for chylous ascites.FERRANDI√âRE:Ferrandi√©re is a researcher who studied the effectiveness of octreotide in treating chylous ascites.SHAPIRO:Shapiro is a researcher who reported on the resolution of chylous ascites after transplantation.AL-ZUBAIRY:Al-Zubairy is a researcher who explored octreotide as a treatment for chylothorax.GUILLEM:Guillem is a researcher who studied postoperative chylothorax and chyloperitoneum.LUTZ:Lutz is a researcher who investigated transjugular intrahepatic portosystemic shunt for chylothorax.ITKIN:Itkin is a researcher who has experience in thoracic duct embolization for chylous effusion.CHYLOUS EFFUSIONS:Chylous effusions are pathological conditions characterized by the accumulation of chyle in body cavities, often treated with dietary modifications.OCTREOTIDE:Octreotide is a medication used to treat various conditions, including chylothorax and chylous ascites, by reducing lymphatic flow.RADICAL NEPHRECTOMY:Radical nephrectomy is a surgical procedure for removing a kidney, which can lead to complications such as chylous ascites.LYMPHOGRAPHY:Lymphography is a medical imaging technique used to visualize the lymphatic system, often employed in cases of lymphatic leakage.THORACIC DUCT EMBOLIZATION:Thoracic duct embolization is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat chylous effusions by blocking the thoracic duct.CHYLE LEAKS:CHYLOUS EFFUSION:HOSPITAL CLINIC:Hospital Cl√≠nic in Barcelona is a medical institution specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, where specialists provide clinical nutrition and dietary services.PERE LEYES I GARC√çA:Pere Leyes i Garc√≠a is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Cl√≠nic, involved in clinical nutrition and dietary management.GEYELIN:Geyelin was a researcher who described the cessation of seizures with absolute fasting in 1921.WILDER:Wilder was a researcher who in 1921 described the ketogenic diet, attributing its anticonvulsant properties to the production of ketone bodies.MAE:MAE, which stands for "medicamentos antiepil√©pticos," is a treatment approach primarily used for managing epilepsy, particularly in patients with refractory epilepsy. While MAE has become the primary treatment option for epilepsy, effectively controlling seizures, it has also led to dietary treatments, such as the ketogenic diet, being considered secondary options. The efficacy of the ketogenic diet can vary among patients, and in some cases, it may still play a role in the overall treatment plan alongside antiepileptic medications.CRISIS EPILEPTICAS:Epileptic seizures are episodes of uncontrolled electrical activity in the brain, which can be managed through various treatments, including dietary approaches.ESCLEROSIS TUBEROSA:Esclerosis tuberosa es un trastorno gen√©tico que provoca el crecimiento de tumores benignos en diversos √≥rganos, incluyendo el cerebro. Esta condici√≥n puede estar asociada con la epilepsia, lo que la convierte en un foco de atenci√≥n en el tratamiento de esta enfermedad. Adem√°s, la esclerosis tuberosa es una de las condiciones para las cuales se aplica la dieta cetog√©nica, un enfoque diet√©tico que ha mostrado beneficios en el manejo de la epilepsia.S√çNDROME DE LENNOX-GASTAUT:Lennox-Gastaut syndrome is a severe form of epilepsy characterized by multiple types of seizures and is treated with the ketogenic diet.GUELPA:GLUT1:El s√≠ndrome de la deficiencia de GLUT1 es un defecto de transporte de glucosa al cerebro que causa epilepsia y retraso en el desarrollo.PIRUVATO DESHIDROGENASA:La deficiencia de piruvato deshidrogenasa es un trastorno metab√≥lico que afecta la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar la glucosa como fuente de energ√≠a.STATUS EPILEPTICUS:Status epilepticus is a serious medical condition characterized by prolonged or repeated seizures without recovery between them. It is considered a medical emergency due to the potential for significant complications. In cases where status epilepticus is refractory to standard treatments, the ketogenic diet may be utilized as a therapeutic option.CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS, or intensive care, refers to the specialized treatment provided to patients who are critically ill. This care is typically administered in intensive care units (ICUs), which are specialized medical facilities designed to offer comprehensive support to these patients. In ICUs, critically ill individuals receive close monitoring of vital signs, including glucose levels, and nutritional support tailored to their specific needs. Additionally, cuidados intensivos encompasses the management of severe medical conditions, such as status epilepticus, ensuring that patients receive the necessary interventions and therapies to stabilize their health.ANTICONVULSIVANTES:Los anticonvulsivantes son medicamentos utilizados para prevenir o tratar las crisis epil√©pticas.CRISIS AT√ìNICAS:Las crisis at√≥nicas son episodios de p√©rdida repentina del tono muscular, lo que puede llevar a ca√≠das o colapsos.CRISIS PARCIALES:Las crisis parciales son crisis epil√©pticas que afectan solo una parte del cerebro y pueden manifestarse de diversas maneras, dependiendo de la regi√≥n afectada.CRISIS T√ìNICO-CL√ìNICAS GENERALIZADAS:Las crisis t√≥nico-cl√≥nicas generalizadas son un tipo de crisis epil√©ptica que involucra contracciones musculares t√≥nicas seguidas de sacudidas cl√≥nicas, afectando todo el cuerpo.EPILEPSIA MIOCL√ìNICA SEVERA DE LA INFANCIA:La epilepsia miocl√≥nica severa de la infancia es un tipo de epilepsia que se presenta en la infancia y se caracteriza por convulsiones miocl√≥nicas frecuentes y severas.ACETAZOLAMIDA:Acetazolamida is a medication that is recommended to be taken on an empty stomach to enhance its absorption. It functions as a carbonic anhydrase inhibitor, which can lead to a significant risk of acidosis if used concurrently with a ketogenic diet.√ÅCIDO VALPROICO:El √°cido valproico es un medicamento que inhibe la Œ≤-oxidaci√≥n y se conjuga con la carnitina acil-transferasa, lo que puede llevar a un d√©ficit de carnitina.HIPERAMONIEMIA:La hiperamonemia es una condici√≥n m√©dica caracterizada por niveles elevados de amon√≠aco en la sangre, que puede ser un efecto secundario en algunos pacientes.EDEMA CEREBRAL:Edema cerebral, or cerebral edema, is the swelling of the brain caused by an accumulation of excess fluid. This condition can arise in severe cases of hyponatremia and is considered a medical emergency that necessitates immediate intervention. Additionally, cerebral edema can be a complication in patients suffering from various metabolic conditions. The presence of excess fluid in the brain can lead to increased intracranial pressure and potentially serious health consequences, highlighting the importance of prompt diagnosis and treatment.CRISIS:Crisis refers to seizures experienced by patients with refractory epilepsy, characterized by episodes of abnormal electrical activity in the brain. The ketogenic diet is designed to reduce or eliminate these seizures in affected individuals. This dietary approach specifically targets the control of these episodes, aiming to improve the quality of life for patients suffering from epilepsy.ENSAYOS CL√çNICOS ALEATORIZADOS:Los ensayos cl√≠nicos aleatorizados son estudios que se utilizan para evaluar la eficacia de la dieta cetog√©nica en comparaci√≥n con grupos de control.REVISI√ìN COCHRANE:La Revisi√≥n Cochrane es un an√°lisis exhaustivo que incluye ensayos cl√≠nicos sobre la eficacia de la dieta cetog√©nica, proporcionando evidencia sobre su uso en pacientes. Adem√°s, se trata de una revisi√≥n sistem√°tica que eval√∫a la efectividad de las f√≥rmulas inmunomoduladoras en pacientes con c√°ncer. En conjunto, estas revisiones reflejan el compromiso de la Revisi√≥n Cochrane con la evaluaci√≥n rigurosa de intervenciones m√©dicas y nutricionales, contribuyendo a la base de evidencia en el √°mbito de la salud.NI√ëOS Y ADOLESCENTES:Los ni√±os y adolescentes son el grupo demogr√°fico m√°s estudiado en relaci√≥n con la dieta cetog√©nica y su eficacia en la reducci√≥n de crisis epil√©pticas.HIPOGLICEMIA HIPOCET√ìSICA:DIETA ATKINS MODIFICADA:La Dieta Atkins Modificada es un enfoque diet√©tico que se caracteriza por la limitaci√≥n de la ingesta de gl√∫cidos. Esta dieta ha sido objeto de varios estudios que eval√∫an su eficacia en el tratamiento de crisis epil√©pticas. Se considera una variante de la dieta cetog√©nica, ya que tambi√©n tiene como objetivo el control de las crisis, aunque se diferencia en las proporciones de macronutrientes que se utilizan.CUMPLIMIENTO:El cumplimiento es el grado en que los pacientes siguen las recomendaciones de la dieta, lo cual afecta la eficacia del tratamiento.EFICACIA:MULTIVITAM√çNICO:Un preparado multivitam√≠nico con minerales y elementos traza es recomendado para evitar carencias en la dieta cetog√©nica.EXCIPIENTES:Los excipientes de los medicamentos pueden influir en la efectividad de la dieta cetog√©nica, siendo importante verificar su contenido.CONTROL AMBULATORIO:El control ambulatorio es necesario durante la realizaci√≥n de la dieta cetog√©nica para asegurar un adecuado desarrollo pondoestatural y evitar complicaciones.JOHNS HOPKINS HOSPITAL:Johns Hopkins Hospital is a medical institution known for its research and treatment protocols, including the classic ketogenic diet for refractory epilepsy.DC:DC refers to a dietary treatment that has been extensively studied for its effects on various health parameters in children, particularly in relation to metabolic disorders and nutritional complications. Specifically, DC is recognized as the classic ketogenic diet, which has served as a standard treatment for refractory epilepsy for many years. This diet is commonly utilized for managing epileptic seizures and has been compared with other dietary approaches, such as the DAM, in several studies.DCSA:DCSA is a modified ketogenic diet without initial fasting, implemented gradually to achieve the desired caloric intake.DGSA:DGSA is a gradual ketogenic diet that progresses the ketogenic ratio from 1:1 to 4:1 over several days.VARIANTES DE DIETAS CETOG√âNICAS:Variants of ketogenic diets include different types and modifications aimed at improving tolerability and effectiveness.HUTTENLOCHER:Huttenlocher is a researcher who initially described the medium-chain triglyceride (MCT) ketogenic diet in 1971.ATKINS DIET:The Atkins diet is a low-carbohydrate diet originally developed for weight loss. It has gained recognition as an alternative for individuals who may find the ketogenic diet too restrictive. In addition to its weight loss benefits, the Atkins diet has also been studied for its potential effectiveness in treating intractable epilepsy.MEDIUM-CHAIN TRIGLYCERIDES:Medium-chain triglycerides (MCTs) are a type of fat that can be used in ketogenic diets to enhance ketosis and improve palatability.CLASSIC KETOGENIC DIET:The classic ketogenic diet is a high-fat, low-carbohydrate diet that has been traditionally used to treat epilepsy.DIETARY PROTOCOL:Dietary protocols are structured plans for implementing specific diets, such as the gradual ketogenic diet protocol described in the text.COLLEGIATE STUDY:A collegiate study refers to research conducted in academic settings, often comparing different dietary approaches for medical conditions.DIETARY THERAPIES:DAM:La DAM es un tratamiento diet√©tico que se utiliza en combinaci√≥n con antiepil√©pticos para reducir la frecuencia de crisis epil√©pticas.LECHE CETOG√âNICA:La Leche Cetog√©nica es un complemento diet√©tico que se utiliza en la dieta cetog√©nica, especialmente para ni√±os y pacientes con secuelas neurol√≥gicas.DIETA DE BAJO √çNDICE GLUC√âMICO:La Dieta de Bajo √çndice Gluc√©mico es una alternativa menos restrictiva a la DC y la DAM, permitiendo solo alimentos con un √≠ndice gluc√©mico inferior a 50.COMPLICACIONES METAB√ìLICAS:Las Complicaciones Metab√≥licas son efectos adversos que pueden surgir durante el tratamiento con dietas cetog√©nicas, incluyendo deshidrataci√≥n y hipoglucemia.CRISIS EPIL√âPTICAS:Las Crisis Epil√©pticas son episodios de actividad el√©ctrica anormal en el cerebro, que pueden ser tratados con dietas como la DAM y la DC.AYUNO INICIAL:El Ayuno Inicial es un protocolo que se utiliza en algunos tratamientos diet√©ticos, que puede influir en la aparici√≥n de complicaciones como la deshidrataci√≥n.SUEROTERAPIA DE MANTENIMIENTO:La Sueroterapia de Mantenimiento es un tratamiento que se utiliza para prevenir la deshidrataci√≥n en pacientes que siguen dietas cetog√©nicas.ESTUDIOS ALEATORIZADOS:HIPOGLUCEMIA GRAVE:Grave hipo glucemia refers to severe and prolonged low blood sugar levels that can occur as a complication of metabolic disorders.HYPERCOLESTEROLIEMIA:Hypercolesterolemia is a condition of elevated cholesterol levels in the blood, frequently observed in patients.HYPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA:Hypertrigliceridemia is a condition characterized by high triglyceride levels in the blood, which has been noted in a significant percentage of patients.COMPLICACIONES DIGESTIVAS:Las complicaciones digestivas son efectos secundarios comunes de la dieta cetog√©nica, incluyendo diarrea, n√°useas y v√≥mitos.COMPLICACIONES CARD√çACAS:Las complicaciones card√≠acas, aunque raras, pueden incluir miocardiopat√≠a y trastornos del ritmo en pacientes en dieta cetog√©nica.CRECIMIENTO LINEAL:El crecimiento lineal en ni√±os tratados con dieta cetog√©nica puede verse afectado, especialmente con una proporci√≥n proteica inadecuada.ESTUDIO DE 6 MESES:Un estudio que evalu√≥ la evoluci√≥n pondoestatural de ni√±os tratados con dieta cetog√©nica durante 6 meses.ESTUDIO DE 15 MESES:Un estudio que compar√≥ el gasto energ√©tico y el crecimiento en ni√±os con dieta cetog√©nica y ni√±os sanos durante 15 meses.ESTUDIO RETROSPECTIVO:"ESTUDIO RETROSPECTIVO" se refiere a un an√°lisis que examina diferentes aspectos relacionados con la dieta cetog√©nica. Este estudio sugiere que el retraso en el crecimiento en ni√±os que siguen una dieta cetog√©nica podr√≠a estar vinculado al aporte proteico que reciben. Adem√°s, el estudio retrospectivo ha encontrado que el uso de citrato pot√°sico est√° asociado con una menor prevalencia de litiasis renal en pacientes que son tratados con esta misma dieta. En conjunto, estos hallazgos destacan tanto las preocupaciones sobre el crecimiento infantil como los beneficios potenciales en la prevenci√≥n de problemas renales en el contexto de la dieta cetog√©nica.N√ÅUSEAS Y V√ìMITOS:N√°useas y v√≥mitos are gastrointestinal symptoms that can arise from the sudden onset of the ketogenic diet, particularly related to the degree of ketosis experienced by individuals.FIBROGASTROSCOPIA:Fibrogastroscopia is a medical procedure utilized to evaluate gastrointestinal health, particularly in patients preparing to begin a ketogenic diet. This procedure enables doctors to visualize the upper digestive tract, which includes the esophagus, stomach, and duodenum. It is instrumental in diagnosing various conditions that may affect these areas, ensuring that any underlying issues are identified and addressed before the initiation of dietary changes.MIOCARDIOPAT√çA:Miocardiopat√≠a is a rare cardiac complication associated with selenium deficiency in patients on a ketogenic diet.PROLONGACI√ìN DEL INTERVALO QT:Prolongaci√≥n del intervalo QT is a cardiac rhythm disorder observed in some children on a ketogenic diet.DESMINERALIZACI√ìN √ìSEA:Desmineralizaci√≥n √≥sea is a risk for patients on a ketogenic diet due to chronic acidosis, leading to potential osteopenia.SUPLEMENTACI√ìN CON CALCIO Y VITAMINA D:Suplementaci√≥n con calcio y vitamina D is recommended for patients on a ketogenic diet to prevent bone demineralization.BAILEY EE:Bailey EE es un autor que ha investigado el uso de la dieta en el tratamiento de la epilepsia, contribuyendo a la literatura m√©dica sobre el tema.PFEIFER HH:Pfeifer HH es un autor que ha colaborado en estudios sobre la dieta cetog√©nica y su eficacia en el tratamiento de la epilepsia.THIELE EA:Thiele EA es un autor que ha investigado el uso de la dieta cetog√©nica en el tratamiento de la epilepsia, aportando a la comprensi√≥n de su eficacia.MARTIN K:Martin K es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci√≥n sobre la dieta cetog√©nica y otros tratamientos diet√©ticos para la epilepsia.JACKSON CF:Jackson CF es un autor que ha colaborado en estudios sobre la dieta cetog√©nica y su efectividad en el tratamiento de la epilepsia.LEVY RG:Levy RG es un autor que ha investigado la dieta cetog√©nica y su uso en el tratamiento de la epilepsia, contribuyendo a la literatura m√©dica.COOPER PN:Cooper PN es un autor que ha trabajado en la investigaci√≥n sobre la dieta cetog√©nica y otros tratamientos diet√©ticos para la epilepsia.KOSSOFF EH:Kossoff E. H. is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his extensive work on the ketogenic diet and its application in treating epilepsy. He has conducted significant studies that explore the efficacy of dietary therapies, particularly the ketogenic diet, in managing this neurological condition. His contributions to the field have been influential in advancing the understanding of how dietary interventions can benefit individuals with epilepsy.ZUPEC-KANIA B:Zupec-Kania B es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci√≥n sobre la dieta cetog√©nica y su aplicaci√≥n en el tratamiento de la epilepsia.ADHERENCIA A LA DIETA:La buena adherencia a la dieta cetog√©nica es un factor determinante en su efectividad para el tratamiento de la epilepsia.VIGILANCIA DE GLUCEMIA:La vigilancia de la glucemia es crucial durante la instauraci√≥n de la dieta cetog√©nica para asegurar la salud del paciente.VIGILANCIA DE HIDRATACI√ìN:La vigilancia del estado de hidrataci√≥n es importante durante el seguimiento de pacientes en la dieta cetog√©nica para prevenir complicaciones.SUPLEMENTACI√ìN CON VITAMINAS Y MINERALES:La suplementaci√≥n con vitaminas y minerales es recomendada para cubrir los requerimientos de los pacientes en la dieta cetog√©nica.MIOCARDIOPAT√çA POR D√âFICIT DE SELENIO:La miocardiopat√≠a por d√©ficit de selenio es una complicaci√≥n potencialmente fatal que puede ocurrir en pacientes en la dieta cetog√©nica.PEDIATRICS:Pediatrics is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to the health and medical care of infants, children, and adolescents. It publishes a wide range of research and reviews focused on child health, including studies on various topics such as vitamin K status in children with cystic fibrosis and the impact of iron deficiency on cognitive achievement among school-aged children. The journal also provides guidelines for the diagnosis and prevention of iron deficiency in infants and young children, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in pediatric health. Overall, Pediatrics serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge and practices related to the health and well-being of children.NORDLI:D. Nordli is a researcher and author who has contributed to the understanding and application of the ketogenic diet in treating epilepsy.FREEMAN:J.M. Freeman is a medical professional known for his work on the ketogenic diet and its efficacy in treating seizure disorders.KINSMA:S.L. Kinsman is a researcher who has studied the efficacy of the ketogenic diet for intractable seizure disorders.KLEPPER:J. Klepper is a researcher who has investigated the effects of the ketogenic diet in various medical conditions, including GLUT1 deficiency syndrome.KOREAN MULTICENTRIC EXPERIENCE:The Korean multicentric experience refers to a study conducted across multiple centers in Korea evaluating the efficacy and safety of the ketogenic diet for intractable childhood epilepsy.SEIZURE DISORDERS:Seizure disorders encompass a range of conditions characterized by recurrent seizures, often treated with various interventions, including the ketogenic diet.GLUT1 DEFICIENCY SYNDROME:J CHILD NEUROL:Journal of Child Neurology publishes research on neurological disorders in children, including studies on the ketogenic diet.LANCET NEUROL:Lancet Neurology is a medical journal that publishes research on neurological conditions, including epilepsy.EPILEPSY BEHAV:Epilepsy & Behavior is a journal that focuses on the behavioral aspects of epilepsy and its treatment.J CLIN NEUROL:Journal of Clinical Neurology publishes clinical research on neurological disorders, including studies on the ketogenic diet.EPILEPSY RES:Epilepsy Research is a journal that publishes research on epilepsy and its treatment options.NEAL EG:Neal E. G. is a researcher actively engaged in multiple studies and clinical trials that evaluate the efficacy of the ketogenic diet for the treatment of epilepsy. His work focuses on comparing different variations of the ketogenic diet to determine their effectiveness in managing this condition.FREEMAN JM:Freeman J. M. is a researcher who has published extensively on the ketogenic diet and its effects on seizure disorders.RATIOS:The study of different lipid:nonlipid ratios in ketogenic diets to evaluate their efficacy and tolerability in epilepsy treatment.MARTINEZ CC:Martinez C. C. is a researcher involved in studies on the ketogenic diet and its effects on seizure disorders.SEO JH:Seo J. H. is a researcher who has studied the efficacy and tolerability of the ketogenic diet in epilepsy treatment.RAJU KNV:Raju K. N. V. is a researcher who has conducted studies comparing different ketogenic diet ratios in treating refractory epilepsy.FUEHRLEIN BS:Fuehrlein B. S. is a researcher who has explored the metabolic effects of ketogenic diets in epilepsy treatment.TALLIAN KB:Tallian K. B. is a researcher who has studied the role of the ketogenic diet in children with intractable seizures.VAN DER LOUW EJTM:Van Der Louw E. J. T. M. is a researcher who has investigated the effects of concomitant lamotrigine use on the ketogenic diet's efficacy.HENDERSON CB:EPILEPSY RESEARCH:Epilepsy Research is a journal that publishes studies related to epilepsy, including dietary interventions like the ketogenic diet.BRAIN DEVELOPMENT:Brain Development is a journal that publishes research on neurological development, including studies on dietary impacts on childhood epilepsy.PEDIATRIC NEUROLOGY:Pediatric Neurology is a journal that focuses on neurological disorders in children, including epilepsy and dietary treatments.SEIZURE:Seizure is a journal that publishes research on seizure disorders, including the effects of dietary interventions.REIF PS:Reif PS is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the ketogenic diet for epilepsy management.BAUER S:Bauer S is a researcher who has worked on the ketogenic diet and its application in treating epilepsy.BELKE M:Belke M is a researcher involved in the study of the ketogenic diet for epilepsy treatment.OERTEL WH:Oertel WH is a researcher who has studied the ketogenic diet's effects on epilepsy.KNAKE S:Knake S is a researcher who has contributed to research on the ketogenic diet and epilepsy.HUTTENLOCHER PR:Huttenlocher PR is a researcher known for studies on the ketogenic diet and its metabolic effects in epilepsy.KAPETANAKIS M:Kapetanakis M is a researcher who has studied the effects of the ketogenic diet on vascular function in epilepsy patients.LIUBA P:Liuba P is a researcher involved in studies on the ketogenic diet and its effects on epilepsy.ODERMARSKY M:Odermarsky M is a researcher who has contributed to research on the ketogenic diet for epilepsy treatment.HALLB√ñ√ñK T:Hallb√∂√∂k T is a researcher who has studied the effects of the ketogenic diet on children with epilepsy.STRZELCZYK A:HOSPITAL SAN JORGE:Hospital San Jorge is a medical facility located in Huesca, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.HOSPITAL GENERAL DE LA DEFENSA:Hospital General de la Defensa is a hospital in Zaragoza, serving as a chief service for endocrinology and nutrition.AMAYA BARRAG√ÅN ANGULO:Amaya Barrag√°n Angulo is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Unit at Hospital San Jorge.MAR√çA LUISA GRACIA RUIZ:Mar√≠a Luisa Gracia Ruiz is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet.VICENTE BLAY CORT√âS:Vicente Blay Cort√©s is the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital General de la Defensa.COREA:Corea es un pa√≠s asi√°tico que recomienda un consumo de sodio de 2 g/d√≠a y de sal de 5 g/d√≠a.INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA CONGESTIVA:Insuficiencia card√≠aca congestiva, tambi√©n conocida como congestive heart failure, es una condici√≥n m√©dica que puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson, una afecci√≥n caracterizada por la acumulaci√≥n de cobre en el organismo que afecta el coraz√≥n. Esta enfermedad se manifiesta con s√≠ntomas como edemas y requiere una restricci√≥n diet√©tica de sodio para mejorar la funci√≥n card√≠aca.GU√çAS AMERICANAS Y CANADIENSES:Las gu√≠as americanas y canadienses recomiendan un consumo de sodio de 1,5 g/d√≠a y de sal de 3,8 g/d√≠a.AM√âRICA:EDEMA C√çCLICO IDIOP√ÅTICO:El edema c√≠clico idiop√°tico es un s√≠ndrome que afecta principalmente a mujeres, caracterizado por episodios de edema y distensi√≥n abdominal.DIETA CONTROLADA EN SODIO:The "DIETA CONTROLADA EN SODIO" refers to a dietary regimen that restricts sodium intake to help manage fluid balance and blood pressure, particularly in patients with renal issues. This controlled sodium diet is essential for individuals dealing with hypertension and other related health problems, as it aids in maintaining overall health and preventing complications associated with excessive sodium consumption.INTERSALT:The INTERSALT study is a significant research initiative that investigates the relationship between sodium consumption and blood pressure. Published in 1988, the study found a clear correlation between sodium intake and blood pressure levels, concluding that a daily sodium intake of 6 grams could lead to reductions in both systolic and diastolic blood pressure. This influential study has contributed to the understanding of how dietary sodium affects cardiovascular health.ALIMENTOS ENLATADOS:Los alimentos enlatados son productos que a menudo contienen sodio como conservante.ALIMENTOS PRECOCINADOS:Los alimentos precocinados son productos que suelen contener sodio para su conservaci√≥n y sabor.ETIQUETADO DE ALIMENTOS:El etiquetado de alimentos es un proceso que informa sobre el contenido de sodio y otros nutrientes en los productos alimenticios.CARNES SALADAS:Refers to salted or cured meats that are discouraged in a low-sodium diet.PESCADOS SALADOS:Refers to salted fish products that are discouraged in a low-sodium diet.QUESOS CURADOS:Refers to aged cheeses that are high in sodium and discouraged in a low-sodium diet.AGUA MINERAL CON GAS:Refers to carbonated mineral water that may contain sodium and is discouraged in a low-sodium diet.ALIMENTOS DESACONSEJADOS:DIETA HIPOS√ìDICA MODERADA:Ejemplo de dieta hipos√≥dica moderada para una persona de 70 a√±os y 70 kg, que incluye varias comidas y alimentos espec√≠ficos para controlar el sodio.DIETA HIPOS√ìDICA ESTRICTA:Ejemplo de dieta hipos√≥dica estricta para un adulto de 70 kg de peso, que detalla comidas y alimentos con bajo contenido de sodio.VINAGRE:El vinagre es un potenciador del sabor recomendado para la cocina sin sal.HIERBAS AROM√ÅTICAS:Las hierbas arom√°ticas son recomendadas para potenciar el sabor de los alimentos en una dieta sin sal.ALIMENTOS RICOS EN SODIO:Los alimentos ricos en sodio deben ser evitados en una dieta hipos√≥dica.CASTA√ëA:La casta√±a es un tipo de fruto seco que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos√≥dica.AVELLANA:La avellana es un tipo de fruto seco que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos√≥dica.COCO DESSECADO:El coco desecado es un tipo de fruta que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos√≥dica.D√ÅTIL SECO:El d√°til seco es un tipo de fruta que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos√≥dica.MELOCOT√ìN SECO:El melocot√≥n seco es un tipo de fruta que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos√≥dica.ALB√ìNDIGAS:Las alb√≥ndigas son un tipo de alimento que se menciona en la dieta hipos√≥dica moderada.PAN SIN SAL:El pan sin sal es un tipo de pan recomendado en las dietas hipos√≥dicas.SOPA:SOPA, or soup, is a type of food that plays a significant role in a strict low-sodium diet. It is recognized for its benefits in hydration and nutrition, particularly during episodes of diarrhea, making it a valuable option for maintaining health in such situations.POLLO ASADO:El pollo asado es un tipo de alimento que se menciona en la dieta hipos√≥dica estricta.ENSALADA:La ensalada es un tipo de comida que se menciona en la dieta hipos√≥dica estricta.CROQUETAS DE PESCADO:Las croquetas de pescado son un tipo de alimento que se menciona en la dieta hipos√≥dica estricta.REQUES√ìN:El reques√≥n es un tipo de queso que se menciona en la dieta hipos√≥dica estricta.PAPILLOTE:M√©todo de cocci√≥n que se recomienda para preparar alimentos en una dieta hipos√≥dica.ESTOFADOS:M√©todo de cocci√≥n que se recomienda para preparar alimentos en una dieta hipos√≥dica.GUISADOS:M√©todo de cocci√≥n que se recomienda para preparar alimentos en una dieta hipos√≥dica.CUIDADO DEL SODIO:El cuidado del sodio es un aspecto importante en la dieta hipos√≥dica, que implica evitar alimentos ricos en sodio.ALMENDRA TOSTADA:DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO:The "DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO" refers to a potassium-controlled diet specifically designed to limit potassium intake. This dietary regimen is particularly important for managing conditions such as hyperkalemia, especially in patients with renal issues. Additionally, the diet plays a crucial role in regulating potassium levels, which is vital for maintaining cardiovascular and muscular health. By controlling potassium intake, individuals can better manage their health conditions and promote overall well-being.DI√ÅLISIS PERITONEAL CONTINUA:Continuous peritoneal dialysis is a treatment that allows for a lower risk of hyperkalemia due to constant therapy.HYPERKALIEMIA:ALIMENTOS INTEGRALES:Alimentos integrales are whole foods that are generally high in potassium and phosphorus, which should be avoided by patients on a restricted diet.PACIENTES EN DI√ÅLISIS:Patients undergoing dialysis who require specific dietary management to maintain their health and prevent complications related to kidney failure.HIPERCALIEMIA:Hipercaliemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated potassium levels in the blood, which can occur in patients with renal failure.DIETA RICA EN POTASIO:A diet that provides at least 100-175 mEq of potassium per day, used for managing and preventing hypokalemia.SISTEMA SCORE:A method developed by European societies for calculating total cardiovascular risk.ESTUDIO FRAMINGHAM:A study that observed the prevalence of hypertension in obese individuals compared to those with normal weight.NATRIURESIS:The process of sodium excretion in the urine, which can be influenced by potassium intake.HYPERTENSI√ìN:A general term for high blood pressure, which includes various forms such as essential and secondary hypertension.PATHS:The PATHS study investigates the effects of alcohol consumption reduction on blood pressure, providing insights into hypertension management.NATIONAL HIGH BLOOD PRESSURE EDUCATION PROGRAM:The National High Blood Pressure Education Program is an initiative designed to educate both the public and healthcare professionals about hypertension, its prevention, and treatment. The program focuses on raising awareness regarding high blood pressure and aims to provide valuable information to help individuals manage and prevent this common health issue.NATIONAL HEART, LUNG AND BLOOD INSTITUTE:The National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) conducts research and provides information on heart, lung, and blood diseases, including hypertension.PA:PA can refer to two distinct medical concepts: blood pressure and pancreatitis. In the context of blood pressure, PA (Presi√≥n Arterial) is a critical factor in diagnosing and managing hypertension, which is essential for maintaining cardiovascular health. On the other hand, PA also denotes pancreatitis, a condition characterized by inflammation of the pancreas that can result in various metabolic disturbances. This condition necessitates careful nutritional support to manage its effects and promote recovery. Thus, PA encompasses both the important measurement of blood pressure and the medical condition of pancreatitis, each with its own implications for health management.ESTUDIO DASH-SODIO:The DASH-sodium study focused on reducing sodium intake in various diets to observe its effects on blood pressure levels.STAMLER:Stamler is a researcher who published findings in 1992 regarding the prevalence of hypertension in primitive societies compared to industrialized ones.CARNES, AVES Y PESCADOS:Carnes, aves y pescados are sources of protein and magnesium, including lean meats and fish.LEGUMBRES Y FRUTOS SECOS:Legumbres y frutos secos are sources of energy, magnesium, potassium, protein, and fiber, including nuts and seeds.JOINT NATIONAL COMMITTEE:The Joint National Committee is a collective that focuses on establishing guidelines for the prevention, detection, evaluation, and treatment of high blood pressure, also known as hypertension. This committee offers comprehensive recommendations for managing hypertension, which include considerations for dietary sodium and potassium intake, among other factors.HTA RESISTENTE A LA SAL:HTA resistente a la sal se refiere a las personas que no experimentan un aumento en la presi√≥n arterial con el consumo de sal.MORTALIDAD CORONARIA:La mortalidad coronaria se refiere a las muertes causadas por enfermedades del coraz√≥n, que pueden verse afectadas por la ingesta de sodio.MORTALIDAD POR ICTUS:La mortalidad por ictus se refiere a las muertes causadas por accidentes cerebrovasculares, que pueden estar influenciadas por la presi√≥n arterial y la ingesta de sodio.DIETA VEGETARIANA:A vegetarian diet is typically rich in polyunsaturated fatty acids and low in saturated fats, which may contribute to lower blood pressure.ACEITES INSATURADOS:Unsaturated oils are fats that can influence blood pressure and are often recommended for a healthy diet.KOREAN NUTRITION SOCIETY:The Korean Nutrition Society is an organization that provides dietary reference intakes and nutritional guidelines for the Korean population.JAPANESE SOCIETY OF HYPERTENSION:The Japanese Society of Hypertension is a professional organization focused on research and guidelines related to hypertension and cardiovascular diseases.TABLAS DE ALIMENTOS:Food tables classify foods into recommended and discouraged categories for patients requiring sodium-controlled diets.EXERCISE F√çSICO:HFSA:Heart Failure Society of America, an organization that provides guidelines for heart failure managementSODIUM-HF:A pilot study investigating the long-term effects of dietary sodium restriction on clinical outcomes in heart failure patientsAM HEART J:AM HEART J, or the American Heart Journal, is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research focused on cardiovascular health. It serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings in the field of cardiology. Notably, in 2003, the journal published a study examining the effects of furosemide and hypertonic saline in the context of heart failure, contributing valuable insights to the understanding and treatment of this condition.BEST PRACT RES CLIN ENDOCRINOL METAB:Best Practice & Research Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism, a journal focusing on endocrinology and metabolismMIDDLE EAST J DIG DIS:Middle East Journal of Digestive Diseases, a publication that discusses issues related to digestive healthSEMIN DIAL:Seminars in Dialysis, a journal that covers topics related to dialysis and kidney healthWORLD HEALTH ORGANISATION:The World Health Organization, a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for international public healthMCMAHON EJ:McMahon EJ is a researcher who has contributed to studies on dietary salt intake for chronic kidney disease patientsNIELS A:Niels A is a researcher who has studied the effects of sodium restriction on various health parametersLINDLEY EJ:EUROPEAN PROSPECTIVE INVESTIGATION INTO CANCER AND NUTRITION:A large-scale study investigating the relationship between diet, nutrition, and cancer across multiple countries in Europe.KAMYAR KALANTAR-ZADEH:A researcher involved in studies related to dietary restrictions in dialysis patients and their nutritional needs.SEMINARS IN DIALYSIS:A journal that focuses on the management and treatment of patients undergoing dialysis, including dietary considerations.EUROPEAN HEART JOURNAL:A leading journal in cardiovascular medicine that publishes guidelines and research related to heart health.AGNOLI C:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.ERICSON U:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.JOHANSSON I:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.FERRARI P:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.ENGESET D:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.LUND E:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.LENTJES M:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.KEY T:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.TOUVIER M:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.NIRAVONG M:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.LARRA√ëAGA N:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.RODR√çGUEZ L:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.OCK√â MC:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.PEETERS PH:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.TJ√òNNELAND A:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.BJERREGAARD L:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.VASILOPOULOU E:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.DILIS V:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.LINSEISEN J:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.N√ñTHLINGS U:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.RIBOLI E:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.SLIMANI N:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake.BINGHAM S:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study.TUMINO R:SCORE PROJECT:The SCORE project is a research initiative focused on estimating the ten-year risk of fatal cardiovascular disease in Europe.DASH COLLABORATIVE RESEARCH GROUP:The DASH Collaborative Research Group is a dedicated team that conducts clinical trials aimed at studying the effects of dietary patterns on blood pressure. Their research focuses on understanding how different dietary approaches can influence blood pressure levels, contributing valuable insights to the field of nutrition and cardiovascular health.INTERSALT STUDY:The INTERSALT Study is a research study that investigates the relationship between sodium intake and blood pressure across different populations.US:The United States is a country where several studies on hypertension and dietary factors have been conducted.WANG RS:Wang RS is a co-author of a study on ambulatory systolic blood pressure in hypertensive smokers.ASCHERIO A:Ascherio A is a researcher involved in a prospective study of nutritional factors and hypertension among US men.GIOVANNUCCI EL:Giovannucci EL is a researcher who contributed to a study on nutritional factors and hypertension among US men.WITTMAN JC:Witteman JC is a researcher who studied nutritional factors and hypertension among US women.SACKS FM:Sacks FM is a researcher involved in studies related to hypertension and dietary factors.HE J:He J is a researcher who studied the long-term effects of weight loss and dietary sodium reduction on hypertension incidence.WHELTON P:Whelton P is a researcher who has contributed to studies on hypertension and dietary factors.CUSHMAN WC:Cushman WC is a researcher involved in the Prevention and Treatment of Hypertension Study (PATHS).FENG J:Feng J is a researcher who studied plasma sodium and its effects on hypertension.TRIALS OF HYPERTENSION PREVENTION COLLABORATIVE RESEARCH GROUP:The Trials of Hypertension Prevention Collaborative Research Group is a dedicated research entity focused on investigating interventions aimed at preventing hypertension. This group conducts comprehensive studies to evaluate the impact of lifestyle changes on the development and management of hypertension, contributing valuable insights into effective prevention strategies.MANN SJ:ANA ISABEL ILUNDAIN GONZ√ÅLEZ:Ana Isabel Ilundain Gonz√°lez is a medical professional affiliated with the Hospital Cl√≠nico Universitario Lozano Blesa, where she specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. She is also a co-author engaged in research related to nephrolithiasis and dietary management, contributing to the understanding of how diet impacts kidney stone formation and overall health.MAR√çA JULIA OC√ìN BRET√ìN:Mar√≠a Julia Oc√≥n Bret√≥n is a medical professional affiliated with the Hospital Cl√≠nico Universitario Lozano Blesa, where she specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical work, she is also an author and researcher, with a particular focus on nephrolithiasis and dietary treatments. Her expertise encompasses both the medical and research aspects of her fields, contributing to advancements in understanding and managing conditions related to nutrition and kidney health.JOS√â ANTONIO GIMENO ORNA:Jos√© Antonio Gimeno Orna is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Cl√≠nico Universitario Lozano Blesa, focusing on endocrinology and nutrition.JORDI PONS DOLSET:Jordi Pons Dolset is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Royo Villanova, focusing on rheumatology.EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF PREVENTIVE CARDIOLOGY:The European Journal of Preventive Cardiology is a journal that publishes research on cardiovascular health and prevention strategies.HORMONAS CALCITROPAS:Las hormonas calciotropas son un grupo de tres hormonas que regulan el metabolismo del calcio en el cuerpo, actuando en el intestino, ri√±√≥n y hueso.GL√ÅNDULAS PARATIROIDES:Las gl√°ndulas paratiroides son gl√°ndulas endocrinas que regulan los niveles de calcio en la sangre mediante la secreci√≥n de hormona paratiroidea.ALCALOSIS METAB√ìLICA:La alcalosis metab√≥lica es un trastorno que tambi√©n puede aumentar la fijaci√≥n del calcio a la alb√∫mina, afectando los niveles de calcio ionizado.CALCIO PLASM√ÅTICO:FGF-23:El FGF-23 es una hormona producida por los osteocitos que tiene un efecto fosfat√∫rico potente, disminuyendo la absorci√≥n intestinal de f√≥sforo.DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO:A controlled calcium diet, known as "DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO," is an approach that emphasizes the regulation of calcium intake to prevent and treat conditions such as osteoporosis and hypercalcemia. This dietary strategy focuses on achieving a balanced nutrient intake, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary amounts of calcium while managing their overall health. By carefully monitoring calcium consumption, this diet aims to support bone health and prevent complications associated with excessive calcium levels.ALUMINIO:Aluminio is a chemical element that serves as a component in certain antacids. It has been noted for its ability to inhibit gastric motility, which can lead to gastrointestinal complications, particularly when combined with enteral nutrition. Additionally, aluminum is associated with toxicity in parenteral nutrition, which can adversely affect bone mass. The element is linked to various medical conditions and poses a risk of intoxication, highlighting the need for caution in its use within medical treatments.TIAZIDAS:TIAZIDAS, or thiazides, are a class of diuretics that play a significant role in influencing the levels of calcium and phosphorus in the body. These medications are known for their ability to retain calcium, which can have various effects on the body's mineral balance.HOSPITALIZADOS:The term "HOSPITALIZADOS" refers to hospitalized patients, who are individuals receiving medical care in a hospital setting. These patients often require nutritional support during their stay to aid in their recovery and overall health management.PACIENTES S√âPTICOS:Patients who are septic are also at increased risk for developing hypophosphatemia.CALCIFICACIONES DE TEJIDOS BLANDOS:Soft tissue calcifications are complications that can arise from prolonged elevated phosphorus levels in patients with chronic kidney disease.)<|COMPLETE|>HUESO:HUESO, which translates to "bone" in English, serves as a major storage site for magnesium in the body, containing approximately 60% of the total body magnesium.CARBONATO DE LANTANO:Lanthanum carbonate is a medication used to reduce phosphate levels in patients with chronic kidney disease.PTH INTACTA:Intact parathyroid hormone (PTH) is a hormone that regulates calcium and magnesium levels in the body.SEVELAMER:ENFERMEDAD DE WHIPPLE:La enfermedad de Whipple es una enfermedad infecciosa que afecta la absorci√≥n intestinal, lo que puede llevar a deficiencias de magnesio.F√ÅRMACOS INHIBIDORES DE LA BOMBA DE PROTONES:Los f√°rmacos inhibidores de la bomba de protones son medicamentos que reducen la producci√≥n de √°cido en el est√≥mago y pueden contribuir a la malabsorci√≥n de magnesio.RESORCI√ìN √ìSEA:La resorci√≥n √≥sea es el proceso por el cual el tejido √≥seo es descompuesto, lo que puede aumentar el riesgo de osteoporosis.FORMACI√ìN √ìSEA:La formaci√≥n √≥sea es el proceso de creaci√≥n de nuevo tejido √≥seo, que se ve afectado por factores hormonales y nutricionales.PROTE√çNA:PROTE√çNA is a macronutrient that plays a crucial role in healing and immune response, making it particularly important in the nutritional management of critically ill patients. However, an excessive intake of protein in the diet can disrupt the balance of electrolytes, including magnesium, potentially leading to a condition known as hypomagnesemia. This highlights the importance of maintaining a balanced protein intake to support health while avoiding negative effects on electrolyte levels.FRAX:Fracture Risk Assessment Tool (FRAX) is a computer tool used to evaluate the risk of fractures in patients, calculating the probability of suffering a fracture within ten years.VITAMIN K:Vitamin K is a fat-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in blood clotting and bone health. It is essential for the proper functioning of various proteins involved in these processes, particularly in the mineralization of the organic matrix of collagen in bones. Vitamin K is often monitored in patients with specific conditions, such as those with FQ (fluoroquinolone) and EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease), as it has particular recommendations for these individuals. Overall, Vitamin K is vital for maintaining both blood coagulation and bone metabolism.TOBACCO:Tobacco is an independent risk factor for fractures, accelerating bone mass loss, especially in women.CAFFEINE:Caffeine can increase urinary calcium excretion, which may affect calcium balance in elderly individuals or postmenopausal women.SEDENTARISM:Sedentarism is a lifestyle factor that can increase the risk of developing osteoporosis.SMOKING:Smoking is a lifestyle factor that contributes to the risk of osteoporosis.DIETARY IMBALANCE:Dietary imbalance, including low calcium intake, is a significant risk factor for osteoporosis.ANTIANDROGENS:Antiandrogens are medications that may increase the risk of osteoporosis.THYROXINE:Excessive doses of thyroxine can lead to osteoporosis.ANTICONVULSANTS:Certain anticonvulsants are associated with an increased risk of osteoporosis.ENDOCRINOPATHIES:Endocrinopathies such as hyperthyroidism and Cushing's disease can contribute to the risk of osteoporosis.MALABSORPTIVE DISEASES:Malabsorptive diseases can lead to osteoporosis due to inadequate nutrient absorption.RENAL DISEASES:Renal diseases can affect bone health and contribute to osteoporosis.(N␀␀␀␀␀␀´N␀␀␀␀␀␀?P␀␀␀␀␀␀’P␀␀␀␀␀␀cQ␀␀␀␀␀␀¯Q␀␀␀␀␀␀R␀␀␀␀␀␀µR␀␀␀␀␀␀1S␀␀␀␀␀␀£V␀␀␀␀␀␀X␀␀␀␀␀␀\Y␀␀␀␀␀␀ÜZ␀␀␀␀␀␀˝[␀␀␀␀␀␀k]␀␀␀␀␀␀„]␀␀␀␀␀␀_^␀␀␀␀␀␀l^␀␀␀␀␀␀_␀␀␀␀␀␀ya␀␀␀␀␀␀*b␀␀␀␀␀␀Ãb␀␀␀␀␀␀xc␀␀␀␀␀␀;e␀␀␀␀␀␀f␀␀␀␀␀␀ùf␀␀␀␀␀␀úi␀␀␀␀␀␀j␀␀␀␀␀␀bj␀␀␀␀␀␀[k␀␀␀␀␀␀“k␀␀␀␀␀␀\l␀␀␀␀␀␀Ál␀␀␀␀␀␀tm␀␀␀␀␀␀n␀␀␀␀␀␀ûn␀␀␀␀␀␀o␀␀␀␀␀␀«o␀␀␀␀␀␀Bp␀␀␀␀␀␀wq␀␀␀␀␀␀Qr␀␀␀␀␀␀Ïr␀␀␀␀␀␀†s␀␀␀␀␀␀Dt␀␀␀␀␀␀Ku␀␀␀␀␀␀îv␀␀␀␀␀␀¨v␀␀␀␀␀␀w␀␀␀␀␀␀zw␀␀␀␀␀␀az␀␀␀␀␀␀}␀␀␀␀␀␀Å}␀␀␀␀␀␀~␀␀␀␀␀␀π␀␀␀␀␀␀EÄ␀␀␀␀␀␀≈Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀Ç␀␀␀␀␀␀œÇ␀␀␀␀␀␀eÉ␀␀␀␀␀␀ÊÉ␀␀␀␀␀␀¢Ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀≈Ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀qÖ␀␀␀␀␀␀Ü␀␀␀␀␀␀≥Ü␀␀␀␀␀␀.á␀␀␀␀␀␀Óâ␀␀␀␀␀␀sä␀␀␀␀␀␀Âä␀␀␀␀␀␀¸ä␀␀␀␀␀␀Sé␀␀␀␀␀␀‹ë␀␀␀␀␀␀sí␀␀␀␀␀␀˘í␀␀␀␀␀␀Éì␀␀␀␀␀␀î␀␀␀␀␀␀¬î␀␀␀␀␀␀nï␀␀␀␀␀␀)ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀◊ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀çó␀␀␀␀␀␀'ò␀␀␀␀␀␀÷ò␀␀␀␀␀␀{ô␀␀␀␀␀␀ôô␀␀␀␀␀␀|ö␀␀␀␀␀␀uú␀␀␀␀␀␀˚ú␀␀␀␀␀␀iù␀␀␀␀␀␀éü␀␀␀␀␀␀†␀␀␀␀␀␀¿†␀␀␀␀␀␀O°␀␀␀␀␀␀f°␀␀␀␀␀␀¢␀␀␀␀␀␀ò¢␀␀␀␀␀␀h§␀␀␀␀␀␀ˆ§␀␀␀␀␀␀é•␀␀␀␀␀␀û•␀␀␀␀␀␀ê¶␀␀␀␀␀␀	ß␀␀␀␀␀␀◊ß␀␀␀␀␀␀C™␀␀␀␀␀␀ø´␀␀␀␀␀␀®≠␀␀␀␀␀␀*Æ␀␀␀␀␀␀‹Æ␀␀␀␀␀␀H≤␀␀␀␀␀␀Ω≤␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇ≤␀␀␀␀␀␀N≥␀␀␀␀␀␀†≥␀␀␀␀␀␀Ô≥␀␀␀␀␀␀N¥␀␀␀␀␀␀Yµ␀␀␀␀␀␀ö∂␀␀␀␀␀␀◊∂␀␀␀␀␀␀0∑␀␀␀␀␀␀z∑␀␀␀␀␀␀„∑␀␀␀␀␀␀∏␀␀␀␀␀␀∫␀␀␀␀␀␀D∫␀␀␀␀␀␀Å∫␀␀␀␀␀␀Áª␀␀␀␀␀␀Ω␀␀␀␀␀␀ÜΩ␀␀␀␀␀␀æ␀␀␀␀␀␀\æ␀␀␀␀␀␀Ôæ␀␀␀␀␀␀ùø␀␀␀␀␀␀_¿␀␀␀␀␀␀¿␀␀␀␀␀␀y¡␀␀␀␀␀␀Ù¡␀␀␀␀␀␀Ñ¬␀␀␀␀␀␀Ó¬␀␀␀␀␀␀a√␀␀␀␀␀␀Ï√␀␀␀␀␀␀fƒ␀␀␀␀␀␀Òƒ␀␀␀␀␀␀\≈␀␀␀␀␀␀È≈␀␀␀␀␀␀Q∆␀␀␀␀␀␀Õ∆␀␀␀␀␀␀>«␀␀␀␀␀␀°«␀␀␀␀␀␀»␀␀␀␀␀␀~»␀␀␀␀␀␀Â»␀␀␀␀␀␀]…␀␀␀␀␀␀∏…␀␀␀␀␀␀! ␀␀␀␀␀␀w ␀␀␀␀␀␀Ú ␀␀␀␀␀␀ˆ ␀␀␀␀␀␀çÃ␀␀␀␀␀␀Õ␀␀␀␀␀␀©œ␀␀␀␀␀␀O–␀␀␀␀␀␀`–␀␀␀␀␀␀—␀␀␀␀␀␀#—␀␀␀␀␀␀/“␀␀␀␀␀␀∆”␀␀␀␀␀␀c‘␀␀␀␀␀␀#’␀␀␀␀␀␀Ù÷␀␀␀␀␀␀∑◊␀␀␀␀␀␀‘Ÿ␀␀␀␀␀␀F⁄␀␀␀␀␀␀Ω⁄␀␀␀␀␀␀D€␀␀␀␀␀␀ÿ€␀␀␀␀␀␀w‹␀␀␀␀␀␀Â‹␀␀␀␀␀␀M›␀␀␀␀␀␀ª›␀␀␀␀␀␀.ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀␀©ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬂ␀␀␀␀␀␀ßﬂ␀␀␀␀␀␀‡␀␀␀␀␀␀h‡␀␀␀␀␀␀Ï‡␀␀␀␀␀␀|·␀␀␀␀␀␀‚␀␀␀␀␀␀v‚␀␀␀␀␀␀Ú‚␀␀␀␀␀␀c„␀␀␀␀␀␀Î„␀␀␀␀␀␀Y‰␀␀␀␀␀␀‹‰␀␀␀␀␀␀TÂ␀␀␀␀␀␀€Â␀␀␀␀␀␀iÊ␀␀␀␀␀␀ÍÊ␀␀␀␀␀␀†Á␀␀␀␀␀␀6Ë␀␀␀␀␀␀ÆË␀␀␀␀␀␀È␀␀␀␀␀␀ÖÈ␀␀␀␀␀␀ıÈ␀␀␀␀␀␀IÍ␀␀␀␀␀␀úÍ␀␀␀␀␀␀Î␀␀␀␀␀␀vÎ␀␀␀␀␀␀”Î␀␀␀␀␀␀-Ï␀␀␀␀␀␀ñÏ␀␀␀␀␀␀¯Ï␀␀␀␀␀␀ûÌ␀␀␀␀␀␀,Ó␀␀␀␀␀␀ªÓ␀␀␀␀␀␀IÔ␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬂÔ␀␀␀␀␀␀ÎÔ␀␀␀␀␀␀¸Ô␀␀␀␀␀