’B=„{ªø1;„±‹:$ó±<=‡º;ù√hº}hüºz≠;ﬂäª§æN=Å"Ñ<_¥È:≈ ›<>ƒK;_ºÜÛ@<°JÑºú»ÅªUa*º,v&ºú:	ªs6<5»<À0Ô:¬•M<îw<.‚<ˇ–=º9Û<∑é<QX:¿,jºw5W=°eΩ;4=Zú;ÇÎª§æŒ<∫ì<¯ZºMµ˛ªo®ªiK␀=Ã≈C=’lV:[«;Ωπ˛∫º.∞ªÁkA<Eø1ºuâ*ºCFŒ;Ô}<=Ø<{"title": "FIBROBLASTS:Fibroblasts are cells that can be cultured to study the oxidation rates of AGCML in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "PLASMA:Plasma is the liquid component of blood that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes. It serves as a medium for transporting nutrients, hormones, and waste products throughout the body. Additionally, plasma is significant in medical diagnostics, as it allows for the measurement of fatty acid levels, which can be instrumental in diagnosing conditions such as adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "AXONOPATHY:Axonopathy is a condition characterized by the degeneration of axons, which is a significant finding in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "ADRENAL INSUFFICIENCY:Adrenal insufficiency is a common complication in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, often requiring steroid treatment."}{"title": "GENE MUTATIONS:Gene mutations related to adrenoleucodistrofia can be studied to aid in diagnosis, although no prevalent mutation has been identified."}{"title": "MORFOLOGICALLY:"}{"title": "ALD:Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD) is a genetic disorder that impacts the metabolism of specific fatty acids, resulting in the buildup of very long-chain fatty acids in the body."}{"title": "RIZZO ET AL:Rizzo et al are researchers who demonstrated the effects of oleic acid on fibroblasts from ALD patients in 1986."}{"title": "ACEITE DE LORENZO:Aceite de Lorenzo is a dietary supplement specifically utilized in the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD), a genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. This treatment aims to normalize plasma concentrations of very long-chain fatty acids, particularly focusing on reducing levels of C26:0 in patients with ALD. The formulation of Aceite de Lorenzo combines glycerol trioleate and glycerol trierucate, which work together to achieve this normalization.\n\nWhile Aceite de Lorenzo has therapeutic benefits, it is important to note that it may also cause side effects, including plaquetopenia (a reduction in platelet count) and a decrease in essential fatty acids. Despite these potential adverse effects, Aceite de Lorenzo remains a significant dietary intervention for managing the symptoms and progression of Adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "GTO:GTO, or glycerol trioleate, is a dietary component utilized in the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). It is recognized as an alternative treatment option that can be continued even if Lorenzo's oil is discontinued due to potential side effects. GTO is notable for its high percentage of oleic acid, which contributes to its therapeutic properties in managing ALD."}{"title": "GTE:GTE, or Glycerol trierucate, is a dietary component characterized by a high percentage of erucic acid. It is utilized in conjunction with GTO for the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). However, it is important to note that GTE treatment may be suspended if patients using Lorenzo's oil experience thrombocytopenia."}{"title": "C26:0:C26:0, also known as hexacosanoic acid, is a very long-chain saturated fatty acid that plays a significant role in the diagnosis of adrenoleucodystrophy (ALD). This fatty acid accumulates in patients suffering from ALD, and efforts are made to reduce its levels through dietary interventions."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO OLEICO:\u00c1cido Oleico is a monounsaturated fatty acid recognized for its safety in emulsions intended for patients requiring nutritional support. Additionally, it has been utilized in fibroblast cultures to lower levels of C26:0 in patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). This dual application highlights its significance in both nutritional and therapeutic contexts."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO ER\u00daCICO:\u00c1cido er\u00facico es un \u00e1cido graso que se encuentra en los l\u00edpidos plaquetarios y est\u00e1 relacionado con la plaquetopenia en pacientes que utilizan aceite de Lorenzo. Este \u00e1cido graso tambi\u00e9n se encuentra en aceites de colza y mostaza, y es importante destacar que los pacientes con adrenoleucodistrofia (ALD) no pueden metabolizarlo adecuadamente."}{"title": "DIETA RESTRINGIDA:The restricted diet is a treatment approach for ALD that limits saturated very long-chain fatty acids."}{"title": "NIVEL PLASM\u00c1TICO:Plasma levels refer to the concentration of fatty acids in the blood, which are monitored in ALD patients."}{"title": "FIBROBLASTOS:"}{"title": "ADRENOLEUCOMIELOPAT\u00cdA:La adrenoleucomielopat\u00eda es una enfermedad neurol\u00f3gica que puede no responder al tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo en estados avanzados."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE DE M\u00c9DULA \u00d3SEA:The \"TRASPLANTE DE M\u00c9DULA \u00d3SEA\" refers to a bone marrow transplant procedure that is sometimes utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions, including Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). This procedure may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition to help reduce infection rates during recovery. While bone marrow transplants have been performed in certain cases of ALD, the effectiveness of this treatment remains uncertain, particularly in advanced stages of the disease. However, it is considered a treatment option for patients who exhibit moderate neurological involvement in ALD."}{"title": "PACIENTES ASINTOM\u00c1TICOS:Los pacientes asintom\u00e1ticos pueden beneficiarse del tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo, que reduce la frecuencia y severidad del deterioro neurol\u00f3gico."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON DISFUNCI\u00d3N ADRENAL:Los pacientes con disfunci\u00f3n adrenal o neurol\u00f3gica preexistente pueden no ver mejoras con el tratamiento de aceite de Lorenzo."}{"title": "VALPROATO:Valproato is a medication that has shown neuroprotective capabilities in animal models for adrenoleucodistrofia and has potential antioxidant effects in patients."}{"title": "LOVASTATINA:Lovastatina, also known as lovastatin, is a medication primarily used to reduce cholesterol levels in the body. Its effectiveness can be influenced by food intake. Additionally, lovastatina has therapeutic applications beyond cholesterol management; it can also reduce AGCML levels in patients suffering from adrenoleucodistrofia. The drug functions by inhibiting nitric oxide synthase, contributing to its diverse pharmacological effects."}{"title": "BETA-INTERFER\u00d3N:Beta-interfer\u00f3n is an immunosuppressive agent that has been tested for reducing inflammatory responses in brain lesions associated with ALD but has not shown significant clinical improvement."}{"title": "MITOXANTRONE:Mitoxantrone is an immunosuppressive agent that has been trialed for treating ALD-related brain lesions without significant success."}{"title": "INMUNOGLOBULINAS:Immunoglobulins, also known as \"inmunoglobulinas,\" are antibodies produced by the immune system that play a crucial role in identifying and neutralizing pathogens such as bacteria and viruses. They are essential components of the immune response and are found in bodily fluids like chyle. In addition to their protective functions, inmunoglobulinas have been investigated as immunosuppressive agents in the treatment of autoimmune liver disease (ALD) to help reduce inflammation. However, studies have indicated that they have not demonstrated significant clinical improvement in this context. Overall, inmunoglobulinas are vital for immune defense while also being explored for their potential therapeutic applications in certain medical conditions."}{"title": "BACLOFENO:Baclofeno is a medication used to treat spasticity as a complication of adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "VIGABATRINA:Vigabatrina is a drug used to treat seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "FENOBARBITAL:Fenobarbital is a medication that enhances penetration into the nervous system and has a delayed elimination effect, which can lead to drowsiness. It is primarily used to control seizures in patients suffering from adrenoleucodystrophy."}{"title": "GENE X-ALD:Gene X-ALD is a gene related to adrenoleucodistrofia that is being researched for gene therapy applications."}{"title": "MITOCONDRIA:Mitochondria are cellular organelles where lipid \u03b2-oxidation occurs, crucial for energy production during fasting and stress."}{"title": "PEROXISOMAS:Peroxisomas are cellular organelles involved in lipid metabolism, particularly in the context of AGCML in adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "LESIONES CEREBRALES:Lesiones cerebrales are brain lesions that occur in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy, leading to neurological symptoms."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO ESTEROIDEO:Tratamiento esteroideo refers to steroid treatment that is essential for managing adrenal function in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "DIETA CONTROLADA:Dieta controlada en \u00e1cidos grasos is a dietary intervention indicated for metabolic disorders affecting lipid oxidation."}{"title": "ESPASTICIDAD:Espasticidad is a condition that can occur as a complication of adrenoleukodystrophy, requiring specific treatment."}{"title": "FUNCION SUPRARRENAL:Funci\u00f3n suprarrenal refers to adrenal function, which is crucial to monitor in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy for appropriate steroid treatment."}{"title": "ESTUDIOS ADICIONALES:Estudios adicionales are further studies required to better understand and treat adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "\u0392-OXIDACI\u00d3N:La \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n es un proceso metab\u00f3lico crucial que descompone \u00e1cidos grasos para producir energ\u00eda. Este proceso puede verse afectado en ciertos trastornos metab\u00f3licos, como la adrenoleucodistrofia, donde se altera la capacidad del organismo para oxidar \u00e1cidos grasos de cadena muy larga."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME REYE-LIKE:El s\u00edndrome Reye-like es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede presentarse en trastornos de la \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n de \u00e1cidos grasos de cadena larga, caracterizada por hipoglucemia y afectaci\u00f3n neurol\u00f3gica."}{"title": "AGCL:Los \u00e1cidos grasos de cadena larga (AGCL) son un tipo de grasa que puede verse afectada en trastornos metab\u00f3licos, especialmente en la \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "AGCM:Los \u00e1cidos grasos de cadena media (AGCM) son un tipo de grasa que se metaboliza de manera diferente y puede ser utilizado en el tratamiento de trastornos de la \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "HIPOGLOCEMIA:La hipoglucemia es una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por niveles bajos de glucosa en la sangre, que puede ser un s\u00edntoma de trastornos de la \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "NEUROPAT\u00cdA:Neuropat\u00eda is a disorder that affects the nerves and can be a symptom of metabolic disorders related to \u03b2-oxidation. It is also recognized as a potential complication of metabolic disorders such as Adrenoleukodystrophy, which impacts nerve function."}{"title": "ARRITMIAS CARD\u00cdACAS:Arritmias card\u00edacas are heart rhythm disorders that can manifest in patients with various metabolic disorders, including Adrenoleukodystrophy. These cardiac arrhythmias are characterized as alterations in the heart's rhythm and may serve as a symptom of disorders related to the \u03b2-oxidation of fatty acids."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS METAB\u00d3LICOS:"}{"title": "C24:0:C24:0 es un \u00e1cido graso que se utiliza en la ratio para el diagn\u00f3stico de adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "C22:0:C22:0 es un \u00e1cido graso que se utiliza en la ratio para el diagn\u00f3stico de adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "TCM:TCM, or Triglycerides of Medium Chain, refers to a type of dietary fat characterized by a chain length of 6 to 12 carbon atoms. These fats are known for their rapid absorption and metabolism in the body, making them beneficial for improving energy absorption and metabolism. TCM is commonly derived from coconut oil and is utilized in various nutritional products aimed at providing energy. Additionally, TCM is significant in dietary treatments, particularly for patients with specific conditions such as adrenoleucodystrophy, where the intake of medium-chain triglycerides may need to be restricted. Furthermore, TCM is used to reduce the intake of omega-6 fatty acids in lipid emulsions, highlighting its role in nutritional management."}{"title": "TCL:TCL is an organization that focuses on dietary modifications and nutritional supplementation, with a particular emphasis on low-fat diets and medium-chain triglycerides (TCM). In the context of nutrition, TCL also refers to Triglycerides of Long Chain, which are dietary fats that require bile salts for absorption and are metabolized differently than TCM. Additionally, TCL is associated with the treatment of nutritional disorders related to \u03b2-oxidation, where long-chain triglycerides play a significant role. Overall, TCL encompasses both the promotion of specific dietary practices and the understanding of different types of triglycerides in nutritional health."}{"title": "MIELINA:La mielina es una sustancia que se acumula an\u00f3malamente en la adrenoleucodistrofia, afectando la funci\u00f3n neurol\u00f3gica."}{"title": "CORTEZA ADRENAL:La corteza adrenal es otra \u00e1rea donde se acumulan \u00e1cidos grasos de cadena muy larga en la adrenoleucodistrofia."}{"title": "ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY:Adrenoleukodystrophy is a genetic disorder that primarily affects lipid metabolism, leading to the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids in the body. This condition has significant impacts on both the nervous system and the adrenal glands, resulting in a range of neurological symptoms. The disorder is characterized by its progressive nature, which can lead to severe complications if not managed appropriately."}{"title": "VAN GEEL BM:Van Geel BM is an author of a study on X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy, focusing on clinical presentation, diagnosis, and therapy."}{"title": "GIR\u00d3S M:Giros M is an author involved in the protocol for diagnosis, treatment, and follow-up of X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "MOSER HW:Moser HW is a researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the study and treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy, particularly focusing on dietary management and the clinical aspects of the condition. His work has been influential in advancing the understanding and therapeutic approaches to this rare genetic disorder."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS DE LA \u0392-OXIDACI\u00d3N:Trastornos de la \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n are metabolic disorders that affect the breakdown of fatty acids and are relevant to the discussion of Adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "HIPOGLUCEMIA NO CET\u00d3SICA:Hipoglucemia no cet\u00f3sica is a symptom associated with metabolic disorders, including those related to Adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "MIOTOPAT\u00cdA:Miopat\u00eda is a condition that can accompany metabolic disorders like Adrenoleukodystrophy, affecting muscle function."}{"title": "AGENTES ANTIINFLAMATORIOS:Agentes antiinflamatorios are medications that have been explored for modifying the inflammatory response in Adrenoleukodystrophy but have shown limited efficacy."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA MUY LARGA:"}{"title": "ADRENOMYELONEUROPATHY:Adrenomyeloneuropathy is a related condition that primarily affects the spinal cord and peripheral nerves, often associated with adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "LORENZO'S OIL:Lorenzo's Oil is a dietary therapy used in the treatment of adrenoleukodystrophy, consisting of a mixture of oleic and erucic acids."}{"title": "JOHN HOPKINS MEDICAL JOURNAL:John Hopkins Med J is a medical journal that publishes research and findings related to various medical conditions, including adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "RIZZO WB:Rizzo WB is a researcher known for his work on fatty acid metabolism and its implications in adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION:Bone Marrow Transplantation is a journal dedicated to publishing research on hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and related fields. The term \"bone marrow transplantation\" refers to a medical procedure that involves administering high doses of chemotherapy followed by the infusion of hematopoietic cells. This procedure is primarily used to treat various conditions, particularly hematological malignancies, where the bone marrow is either replaced or supplemented. Additionally, bone marrow transplantation serves as a treatment option for several genetic disorders, such as adrenoleukodystrophy, with the goal of restoring normal function in the central nervous system."}{"title": "KISHIMOTO Y:Kishimoto Y is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of fatty acid abnormalities in adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "VAN DUYN MA:Van Duyn MA is a researcher involved in studies related to dietary therapies for adrenoleukodystrophy."}{"title": "FATTY ACID ABNORMALITY:"}{"title": "QUILOT\u00d3RAX:QUILOT\u00d3RAX is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can manifest as a pleural effusion and may lead to symptoms such as dyspnea (difficulty breathing) and cough. Chylothorax can occur spontaneously or as a result of trauma, often linked to surgical procedures or disorders of the lymphatic system. Treatment for QUILOT\u00d3RAX typically involves dietary modifications, including specific diets aimed at managing fat metabolism, as well as various medical interventions. These interventions may include surgical techniques and interventional radiology, depending on the underlying cause of the condition. Overall, careful management is essential to address the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural cavity and to alleviate associated symptoms."}{"title": "ASCITIS QUILOSA:Ascitis quilosa is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of chyle, a lymphatic fluid, in the abdominal cavity. This condition often arises due to the rupture or obstruction of abdominal lymphatic ducts and is typically observed around the fifth postoperative day when patients have begun an oral diet. Ascitis quilosa can lead to significant nutritional deficiencies and may necessitate dietary modifications or surgical intervention. It is associated with various medical conditions and can cause symptoms such as abdominal distension. Treatment approaches for ascitis quilosa may include conservative management or surgical options, depending on the severity and underlying causes. In summary, ascitis quilosa involves the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the peritoneal cavity, requiring specific medical and dietary management to address the associated complications."}{"title": "M.\u00aa NURIA VIRGILI CASAS:M.\u00aa Nuria Virgili Casas is a medical professional involved in the study and treatment of nutritional and metabolic disorders."}{"title": "RAFAEL L\u00d3PEZ URDIALES:Rafael L\u00f3pez Urdiales is a medical professional contributing to research in clinical nutrition and metabolism."}{"title": "EVA MAR\u00cdA GARC\u00cdA RAIMUNDO:Eva Mar\u00eda Garc\u00eda Raimundo is a medical professional focused on nutrition and dietetics in clinical settings."}{"title": "M\u00d3NICA MONTSERRAT GIL DE BERNAB\u00c9:M\u00f3nica Montserrat Gil de Bernab\u00e9 is a medical professional working in the field of nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI DE BELLVITGE:Hospital Universitari de Bellvitge is a hospital located in Hospitalet de Llobregat, Barcelona, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "GAUCHER DISEASE TYPE III:Gaucher disease type III is a genetic disorder that affects the body's ability to break down certain fats, leading to various health complications."}{"title": "HURLER SYNDROME:Hurler syndrome is a genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme needed to break down glycosaminoglycans, leading to various physical and cognitive impairments."}{"title": "MAROTEAUX-LAMY SYNDROME:Maroteaux-Lamy syndrome is a genetic disorder that affects connective tissue and is characterized by skeletal abnormalities and other systemic issues."}{"title": "SLY SYNDROME:Sly syndrome is a rare genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that leads to the accumulation of certain substances in the body, affecting various organs."}{"title": "MANNOSIDOSIS:Mannosidosis is a genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that breaks down mannosaccharides, leading to various health issues."}{"title": "FUCOSIDOSIS:Fucosidosis is a rare genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that breaks down fucose, leading to a range of symptoms including neurological issues."}{"title": "ASPARTYGLUCOSAMINURIA:Aspartylglucosaminuria is a genetic disorder characterized by the accumulation of aspartylglucosamine, leading to various health complications."}{"title": "X-LINKED ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY:"}{"title": "CONDUCTO TOR\u00c1CICO:El conducto tor\u00e1cico es un conducto linf\u00e1tico que transporta la linfa desde el sistema linf\u00e1tico al sistema venoso, desembocando en la confluencia de la vena subclavia y la vena yugular interna izquierdas."}{"title": "SISTEMA LINF\u00c1TICO:The \"SISTEMA LINF\u00c1TICO\" is a vital system in the body responsible for transporting lymph, a fluid that contains white blood cells and various other components, through lymphatic vessels to the circulatory system. It is a complex network of tissues and organs that plays a crucial role in the body's immune function by helping to eliminate toxins, waste, and other unwanted materials. This system is essential for maintaining overall health and supporting the body's defense mechanisms."}{"title": "CARCINOMATOSIS PERITONEAL:Peritoneal carcinomatosis refers to the spread of cancer to the peritoneum, which can cause ascitis quilosa."}{"title": "SARCOMA DE KAPOSI:Kaposi's sarcoma is a type of cancer that can lead to complications such as ascitis quilosa."}{"title": "AMILOIDOSIS:Amyloidosis is a disease characterized by the accumulation of amyloid proteins in various organs, which can lead to serious health conditions. This condition can result in complications such as ascitis quilosa and is associated with chronic intestinal pseudo-obstruction, affecting multiple organs, including the gastrointestinal system. The buildup of these abnormal proteins can impair the function of the intestines, potentially affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating the use of parenteral nutrition for affected individuals."}{"title": "LINFANGIOLEIOMATOSIS:Lymphangioleiomyomatosis is a rare lung disease that can cause chylothorax and may be associated with ascitic conditions."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS VENA SUBCLAVIA IZQUIERDA:Left subclavian vein thrombosis can lead to complications affecting lymphatic drainage, potentially resulting in ascitis quilosa."}{"title": "BOCIO ENDOTOR\u00c1CICO:Endothoracic goiter is a condition that can cause obstruction of lymphatic flow, potentially leading to ascitic conditions."}{"title": "QUILOT\u00d3RAX CONG\u00c9NITO:"}{"title": "TORACOCENTESIS:La toracocentesis es un procedimiento m\u00e9dico utilizado para extraer l\u00edquido del espacio pleural, que puede ayudar en el diagn\u00f3stico del quilot\u00f3rax."}{"title": "PARACENTESIS:La paracentesis es un procedimiento m\u00e9dico para extraer l\u00edquido del abdomen, utilizado en el diagn\u00f3stico de ascitis quilosa."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS MICROBIOL\u00d3GICO:AN\u00c1LISIS MICROBIOL\u00d3GICO refers to a microbiological analysis procedure that is essential for various medical evaluations. This analysis is particularly important in clinical settings, as it can be necessary to rule out infections in cases such as pleural effusion or ascites. Additionally, microbiological analysis plays a crucial role in the evaluation of enteral nutrition products, ensuring their safety and efficacy for patient use."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICAS DE IMAGEN:Las t\u00e9cnicas de imagen son m\u00e9todos utilizados para diagnosticar y localizar lesiones en condiciones como el quilot\u00f3rax."}{"title": "LINFOGRAF\u00cdA:La linfograf\u00eda es una t\u00e9cnica de imagen utilizada para evaluar el sistema linf\u00e1tico y puede ser \u00fatil en el diagn\u00f3stico de quilot\u00f3rax."}{"title": "DERRAME PLEURAL:"}{"title": "LINFOCITOS T:LINFOCITOS T, or T lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell that play a central role in cell-mediated immunity. They are crucial for the immune response, helping the body to identify and eliminate pathogens and infected cells."}{"title": "LINFOCITOS B:B lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell that produce antibodies and are essential for humoral immunity."}{"title": "QUILOT\u00d3RAX ASOCIADO A TUMOR:Quilot\u00f3rax associated with a tumor refers to the condition of lymphatic fluid accumulation in the pleural cavity that is linked to the presence of a tumor, affecting prognosis."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL\u00d3GICO:The entity \"TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL\u00d3GICO\" refers to pharmacological treatment, which involves the use of medications to manage various medical conditions. Specifically, it includes the administration of drugs such as somatostatin or octreotide, which are utilized to address conditions like quilot\u00f3rax (chylothorax) and ascitis quilosa (chylous ascites). Additionally, pharmacological treatment may also affect a patient's ability to receive enteral nutrition, indicating that the use of these medications can have implications for nutritional management in patients undergoing such treatments."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR:\"TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR\" refers to a management approach that employs non-surgical methods to address medical conditions such as chylothorax and chylous ascites. This treatment strategy emphasizes dietary modifications and medical therapies as initial interventions, prioritizing resolution of the condition without resorting to invasive surgical options."}{"title": "DIETA MODIFICADA:The \"DIETA MODIFICADA\" refers to a therapeutic dietary approach specifically designed to manage conditions such as quilot\u00f3rax and ascitis quilosa. This modified diet focuses on reducing the intake of long-chain triglycerides while supplementing with medium-chain triglycerides. The primary goal of the dieta modificada is to address the unique nutritional needs associated with these health conditions, promoting better health outcomes through careful dietary management."}{"title": "TEJIDOS PERIF\u00c9RICOS:Tejidos perif\u00e9ricos refers to peripheral tissues in the body where fatty acids are transported and utilized."}{"title": "ALIMENTARY SUPPLEMENTATION:Nutritional supplementation with TCM is a dietary approach aimed at enhancing energy intake and improving the organoleptic properties of low-fat diets."}{"title": "LIPIDS:LIPIDS are a group of fats that play a crucial role in nutrition and energy supply. They are particularly important in medical settings, such as in patients with prolonged stays in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU), where lipid emulsions serve as a source of energy and essential fatty acids. The evaluation of lipids focuses on their fatty acid composition and stability, especially in nutritional products designed for various dietary needs. In the context of pancreatitis, lipids can be administered intravenously; however, their use is controversial due to potential complications that may arise. Additionally, dietary advice regarding the selection of foods in modified diets often emphasizes the importance of long-chain and medium-chain triglycerides, highlighting the diverse applications and considerations surrounding lipids in both clinical and dietary contexts."}{"title": "ZUMOS DE FRUTAS Y VERDURAS:Fruit and vegetable juices are allowed in the modified diet as part of the beverage group."}{"title": "INFUSIONES:Infusions are permitted beverages in the modified diet."}{"title": "REFRESCOS:Sodas are allowed in the modified diet as part of the beverage group."}{"title": "PASTA ITALIANA SIN HUEVO:Egg-free Italian pasta is permitted in the modified diet."}{"title": "S\u00c9MOLA:Semolina is included in the permitted food items for the modified diet."}{"title": "GALLETAS INTEGRALES SIN GRASA:Whole grain cookies without fat are allowed in the modified diet."}{"title": "PESCADO BLANCO:PESCADO BLANCO refers to white fish, which is permitted in modified diets. It is traditionally recommended due to its lower phosphorus content when compared to blue fish, making it a favorable choice for those needing to manage their phosphorus intake."}{"title": "MOLUSCOS Y CRUST\u00c1CEOS:MOLUSCOS Y CRUST\u00c1CEOS, which refers to shellfish and crustaceans, are known to be high in purines, which can lead to elevated uric acid levels in the body. However, they are permitted in modified diets, indicating that their consumption can be managed or included under certain dietary guidelines."}{"title": "CLARA DE HUEVO:Egg whites are permitted in the modified diet."}{"title": "MERMELADA:Jam is permitted in the modified diet as part of the sweets and desserts group."}{"title": "HELADOS DE AGUA:Water-based ice creams are permitted in the modified diet."}{"title": "PASTELER\u00cdA CASERA:Homemade pastries are allowed in the modified diet if made with permitted ingredients."}{"title": "MANTECA DE CERDO:Lard is not allowed in the modified diet."}{"title": "CARNES GRASAS:CARNES GRASAS refers to fatty meats that are characterized by their high fat content. These meats should be limited in children's diets to promote better health outcomes, as they can contribute to various health issues. Additionally, CARNES GRASAS are high in purines, which can lead to increased uric acid levels in the body. Due to these health concerns, fatty meats are not permitted in modified diets, emphasizing the need for careful dietary management to ensure overall well-being."}{"title": "GANSO:Goose is not permitted in the modified diet."}{"title": "V\u00cdSCERAS:Organ meats are not permitted in the modified diet."}{"title": "YEMA DE HUEVO:YEMA DE HUEVO, or egg yolk, is characterized by a high phosphorus content, exceeding 30 mg/g. Due to this elevated phosphorus ratio, it is recommended that egg yolk be limited in consumption. Furthermore, in the context of a modified diet, egg yolk is not permitted, indicating that individuals following such a diet should avoid its inclusion."}{"title": "PESCADO AZUL:PESCADO AZUL refers to blue fish, which is generally discouraged in dietary recommendations due to its higher phosphorus content. However, it is noted that some blue fish may have a favorable phosphorus to protein ratio. Despite this, in the context of a modified diet, blue fish is not permitted."}{"title": "PESCADO O MARISCO ENLATADO EN ACEITE:Canned fish or seafood in oil is not permitted in the modified diet."}{"title": "CHOCOLATES:Chocolates are not permitted in the modified diet, as they are discouraged due to their high phosphorus and potassium content."}{"title": "PASTELER\u00cdA EN GENERAL:General pastries are not allowed in the modified diet."}{"title": "REPOSTER\u00cdA CASERA O COMERCIAL:Homemade or commercial pastries containing prohibited ingredients are not allowed in the modified diet.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "ACEITE MCT:El Aceite MCT es un preparado de triglic\u00e9ridos de cadena media utilizado en dietas para proporcionar energ\u00eda y nutrientes a pacientes con necesidades especiales."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS DEL CONDUCTO TOR\u00c1CICO:Las f\u00edstulas del conducto tor\u00e1cico son condiciones m\u00e9dicas que pueden requerir tratamiento nutricional especializado, como la nutrici\u00f3n enteral o parenteral."}{"title": "ACEITE MCT\u00ae:Aceite MCT\u00ae is a nutritional supplement with a high percentage of medium-chain triglycerides (MCT), used for various dietary needs."}{"title": "LIQUIGEN\u00ae:Liquigen\u00ae is a nutritional supplement that contains a moderate percentage of MCT, designed for specific dietary requirements."}{"title": "MCT DUOCAL\u00ae:MCT Duocal\u00ae is a nutritional product with a significant MCT content, aimed at providing energy and nutrition."}{"title": "MCT M\u00c1S ESENCIALES\u00ae:MCT M\u00c1S ESENCIALES\u00ae is a clinical nutrition product that contains a high percentage of MCT, used for dietary management."}{"title": "MCT NM\u00ae:MCT NM\u00ae is a concentrated nutritional supplement with 100% MCT, used for specific dietary needs."}{"title": "MCT PROCAL\u00ae:MCT PROCAL\u00ae is a nutritional supplement with a high percentage of MCT, designed for energy provision."}{"title": "FORTIMEL JUCY\u00ae:Fortimel Jucy\u00ae is a nutritional drink that provides energy and protein, suitable for patients with specific dietary needs."}{"title": "ENSURE JUCE\u00ae:Ensure Juce\u00ae is a nutritional supplement that offers energy and protein, formulated for dietary management."}{"title": "PROVIDEXTRA DRINK\u00ae:Providextra Drink\u00ae is a nutritional beverage that provides energy and protein, aimed at specific dietary requirements."}{"title": "MONOGEN\u00ae:Monogen\u00ae is a complete nutritional formula with a high content of MCT, used for dietary support."}{"title": "NOVASOURCE PEPTIDE JUNIOR\u00ae:Novasource Peptide Junior\u00ae is a pediatric nutritional formula designed for children with specific dietary needs."}{"title": "EMSOGEN\u00ae:Emsogen\u00ae is a nutritional formula with a high percentage of MCT, used for dietary management."}{"title": "DIETGRIF HIPERPROTEICO\u00ae:Dietgrif hiperproteico\u00ae is a high-protein nutritional formula designed for specific dietary needs."}{"title": "DIETGRIF MCT\u00ae:Dietgrif MCT\u00ae is a nutritional formula with a significant MCT content, aimed at providing energy."}{"title": "NUTRISON MCT\u00ae:Nutrison MCT\u00ae is a nutritional product that contains MCT, used for dietary support."}{"title": "FRESUBIN HP ENERGY\u00ae:Fresubin HP Energy\u00ae is a high-protein nutritional formula designed for energy provision."}{"title": "DIETGRIF ENERG\u00c9TICO\u00ae:Dietgrif energ\u00e9tico\u00ae is a nutritional formula aimed at providing energy and nutrition."}{"title": "NOVASOURCE PEPTIDE\u00ae:Novasource Peptide\u00ae is a nutritional formula designed for specific dietary needs."}{"title": "NUTRISON ADVANCED PEPTISORB\u00ae:Nutrison Advanced Peptisorb\u00ae is a specialized nutritional formula for dietary management."}{"title": "SURVIMED OPD\u00ae:Survimed OPD\u00ae is a nutritional product designed for specific dietary needs."}{"title": "VITAL P\u00c9PTIDO 1.5\u00ae:Vital P\u00e9ptido 1.5\u00ae is a nutritional formula aimed at providing energy and protein."}{"title": "ALITRAQ\u00ae:Alitraq\u00ae is a nutritional product designed for specific dietary management."}{"title": "FRESENIUS:Fresenius is a healthcare group that provides products and services for dialysis, hospital, and nutritional care."}{"title": "SHS:"}{"title": "OCTREOTIDA:Octreotide is a synthetic analog of somatostatin, primarily utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions, including quilot\u00f3rax and ascitis quilosa. It is often administered through continuous infusion. In addition to its standalone use, octreotide is also employed in conjunction with dietary treatments to help reduce lymphatic flow, thereby enhancing clinical outcomes for patients."}{"title": "ETILNEFRINA:Etilnefrina is a sympathomimetic drug that reduces lymphatic flow in the thoracic duct by contracting the smooth muscle of its wall."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO QUIR\u00daRGICO:The entity \"TRATAMIENTO QUIR\u00daRGICO\" refers to surgical treatment options indicated for various medical conditions. Specifically, surgical treatment is recommended for patients suffering from severe pancreatic conditions, especially in cases where complications arise, such as bile duct obstruction or the presence of pseudo cysts. Additionally, surgical intervention is advised for refractory cases of chylothorax and chylous ascites, which involves procedures aimed at repairing injuries to the lymphatic ducts. This comprehensive approach highlights the critical role of surgical treatment in managing complex medical issues."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS LINF\u00c1TICAS:Lymphatic fistulas are abnormal connections that can form between lymphatic vessels and other structures, often requiring surgical intervention."}{"title": "FLUJO LINF\u00c1TICO:"}{"title": "EMBOLIZACI\u00d3N:Embolization is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat conditions such as quilot\u00f3rax and lymphatic fistulas, showing high success rates in traumatic cases."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS QUILOSAS:"}{"title": "CHYLOUS ASCITES:Chylous ascites is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the abdominal cavity. This condition often necessitates specific diagnosis and management strategies to address the underlying causes and alleviate symptoms."}{"title": "CHYLOTHORAX:Chylothorax is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can arise due to various factors, including trauma or complications from surgical procedures. Management of chylothorax often necessitates specific nutritional support to address the underlying issues associated with the accumulation of this fluid."}{"title": "HEAD & NECK:Head & Neck is a medical journal that publishes research related to surgery and treatment of head and neck conditions, including chylous leakage."}{"title": "EUR J CARDIOTHORACIC SURG:Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg is a journal that publishes articles on surgical techniques and management of thoracic and cardiovascular conditions, including chylothorax."}{"title": "ARCH SURG:Arch Surg is a journal dedicated to the field of surgery, encompassing a wide range of surgical practices and research. It publishes studies that address various aspects of surgical care, including postoperative complications such as chylous ascites, as well as topics related to immunonutrition. Through its contributions, Arch Surg aims to advance the understanding and application of surgical techniques and patient management in the medical community."}{"title": "MAYO CLINIC PROC:Mayo Clinic Proceedings is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews on various medical topics, including pleural liquid characteristics of chylothorax."}{"title": "BRITISH JOURNAL OF COMMUNITY NURSING:The British Journal of Community Nursing (Br J Comun Nurs) is a scholarly journal dedicated to the exploration and discussion of community nursing practices. It focuses on various aspects of community nursing, including the management of nutritional issues related to chyle leaks and chylous effusions. The journal publishes a range of research articles and discussions that contribute to the field of community nursing, emphasizing the importance of effective nutritional management within this context."}{"title": "ALLEN DB:Allen dB is an author who co-authored the collective review on chylous ascites published in Surgery 2000."}{"title": "ORGAN C.H:Organ C.H is an author who contributed to the collective review on chylous ascites published in Surgery 2000."}{"title": "NAIR S.K:Nair S.K is an author who wrote about the aetiology and management of chylothorax in adults in Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg 2007."}{"title": "PETKO M:Petko M is an author who co-authored the article on the aetiology and management of chylothorax in adults in Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg 2007."}{"title": "HAYWARD M.P:Hayward M.P is an author who contributed to the article on the aetiology and management of chylothorax in adults in Eur J Cardiothoracic Surg 2007."}{"title": "SMOKE A:Smoke A is an author who discussed the consensus on management of chyle leaks in Nutr Clin Pract 2008."}{"title": "DE LEGGE MH:De Legge MH is an author who co-authored the article on chyle leaks in Nutr Clin Pract 2008."}{"title": "JOHNSTONE DW:Johnstone DW is an author who wrote about postoperative chylothorax in Chest Surg Clin N Am 2002."}{"title": "MCGRATH EE:McGrath EE is an author who discussed chylothorax in the article published in Respiratory Medicine 2010."}{"title": "ALEXANDRAKIS M.G:Alexandrakis M.G is an author who wrote about pleural effusions in hematologic malignancies in Chest 2004."}{"title": "B\u00dcTIKER V:B\u00fctiker V is an author who discussed chylothorax in children in the guidelines published in Chest 1999."}{"title": "KUZDZAL J:Kuzdzal J is an author who wrote about lymphangioleiomyomatosis presenting as a refractory chylothorax in J Cardiovasc Surg 2005."}{"title": "ABLANK CJ:Ablan CJ is an author who reported on postoperative chylous ascites in Arch Surg 1990."}{"title": "LATERRE PF:Laterre PF is an author who discussed chylous ascites in Acta Gastroenterol Belg 2000."}{"title": "LEIBOVITCH I:Leibovitch I is an author who wrote about the diagnosis and management of postoperative chylous ascites in J Urol 2002."}{"title": "MANOLITSAS T.P:Manolitsas T.P is an author who discussed chylous ascites following treatment for gynecologic malignancies in Gynecol Oncol 2002."}{"title": "YOL S:Yol S is an author who reported a rare complication of D3 dissection for gastric carcinoma: chyloperitoneum in Gastric Cancer 2005."}{"title": "SKOURAS V:Skouras V is an author who discussed the diagnosis approach for chylothorax in Curr Opin Pulm Med 2010."}{"title": "MALDONADO F:Maldonado F is an author who wrote about pleural liquid characteristics of chylothorax in Mayo Clinic Proc 2009."}{"title": "AGRAWAL V:Agrawal V is an author who discussed pleural liquid analysis in chylous pleural effusion in Chest 2008."}{"title": "BENDER B:Bender B is an author who wrote about the changing management of chylothorax in the modern era in Eur J Cardiothorac Surg 2016."}{"title": "SRIRAM K:Sriram K is an author who discussed nutritional support in adults with chyle leaks in Nutrition 2016."}{"title": "SAPIN DA:Sapin DA is an author who wrote about chylothorax and chylous ascites in the ASPEN Nutrition Support Core Curriculum 2007."}{"title": "SCHILD HH:Schild HH is an author who discussed treatment options in patients with chylothorax in Dtsch Arztebl Int 2013."}{"title": "WENIGER M:Weniger M is an author who wrote about treatment options for chylous ascites after major abdominal surgery in Am J Surg 2016."}{"title": "MC CRAY S:Mc Cray S is an author who provided an update on nutritional management of chyle leaks in Nutrition Issues in Gastroenterology 2011."}{"title": "BIBBY AC:Bibby AC is an author who discussed nutritional management in chyle leaks and chylous effusions in Br J Comun Nurs 2014."}{"title": "ALFANO V:Alfano V is an author who discussed stable reversal of pathologic signs of primitive intestinal lymphangiectasia with hypolipidic diet in a medical publication.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "PRACTICAL GASTROENTEROLOGY:Practical Gastroenterology is a publication that discusses various topics related to gastrointestinal health and nutrition."}{"title": "ALFANO:Alfano is a researcher who contributed to studies on nutritional management in chyle leaks and chylous effusions."}{"title": "TRITTO:Tritto is a researcher involved in the study of dietary modifications for health conditions."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA RAIMUNDO:Garc\u00eda Raimundo is a researcher who co-authored studies on controlled diets in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ BROCCA:Mart\u00ednez Brocca is a researcher focused on nutritional support in specific medical conditions."}{"title": "KELLY:Kelly is a researcher who studied the management of postoperative chylothorax."}{"title": "HUANG:Huang is a researcher who investigated treatment options for chylous ascites."}{"title": "FERRANDI\u00c9RE:Ferrandi\u00e9re is a researcher who studied the effectiveness of octreotide in treating chylous ascites."}{"title": "SHAPIRO:Shapiro is a researcher who reported on the resolution of chylous ascites after transplantation."}{"title": "AL-ZUBAIRY:Al-Zubairy is a researcher who explored octreotide as a treatment for chylothorax."}{"title": "GUILLEM:Guillem is a researcher who studied postoperative chylothorax and chyloperitoneum."}{"title": "LUTZ:Lutz is a researcher who investigated transjugular intrahepatic portosystemic shunt for chylothorax."}{"title": "ITKIN:Itkin is a researcher who has experience in thoracic duct embolization for chylous effusion."}{"title": "CHYLOUS EFFUSIONS:Chylous effusions are pathological conditions characterized by the accumulation of chyle in body cavities, often treated with dietary modifications."}{"title": "OCTREOTIDE:Octreotide is a medication used to treat various conditions, including chylothorax and chylous ascites, by reducing lymphatic flow."}{"title": "RADICAL NEPHRECTOMY:Radical nephrectomy is a surgical procedure for removing a kidney, which can lead to complications such as chylous ascites."}{"title": "LYMPHOGRAPHY:Lymphography is a medical imaging technique used to visualize the lymphatic system, often employed in cases of lymphatic leakage."}{"title": "THORACIC DUCT EMBOLIZATION:Thoracic duct embolization is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat chylous effusions by blocking the thoracic duct."}{"title": "CHYLE LEAKS:"}{"title": "CHYLOUS EFFUSION:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL CLINIC:Hospital Cl\u00ednic in Barcelona is a medical institution specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, where specialists provide clinical nutrition and dietary services."}{"title": "PERE LEYES I GARC\u00cdA:Pere Leyes i Garc\u00eda is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Cl\u00ednic, involved in clinical nutrition and dietary management."}{"title": "GEYELIN:Geyelin was a researcher who described the cessation of seizures with absolute fasting in 1921."}{"title": "WILDER:Wilder was a researcher who in 1921 described the ketogenic diet, attributing its anticonvulsant properties to the production of ketone bodies."}{"title": "MAE:MAE, which stands for \"medicamentos antiepil\u00e9pticos,\" is a treatment approach primarily used for managing epilepsy, particularly in patients with refractory epilepsy. While MAE has become the primary treatment option for epilepsy, effectively controlling seizures, it has also led to dietary treatments, such as the ketogenic diet, being considered secondary options. The efficacy of the ketogenic diet can vary among patients, and in some cases, it may still play a role in the overall treatment plan alongside antiepileptic medications."}{"title": "CRISIS EPILEPTICAS:Epileptic seizures are episodes of uncontrolled electrical activity in the brain, which can be managed through various treatments, including dietary approaches."}{"title": "ESCLEROSIS TUBEROSA:Esclerosis tuberosa es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que provoca el crecimiento de tumores benignos en diversos \u00f3rganos, incluyendo el cerebro. Esta condici\u00f3n puede estar asociada con la epilepsia, lo que la convierte en un foco de atenci\u00f3n en el tratamiento de esta enfermedad. Adem\u00e1s, la esclerosis tuberosa es una de las condiciones para las cuales se aplica la dieta cetog\u00e9nica, un enfoque diet\u00e9tico que ha mostrado beneficios en el manejo de la epilepsia."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE LENNOX-GASTAUT:Lennox-Gastaut syndrome is a severe form of epilepsy characterized by multiple types of seizures and is treated with the ketogenic diet."}{"title": "GUELPA:"}{"title": "GLUT1:El s\u00edndrome de la deficiencia de GLUT1 es un defecto de transporte de glucosa al cerebro que causa epilepsia y retraso en el desarrollo."}{"title": "PIRUVATO DESHIDROGENASA:La deficiencia de piruvato deshidrogenasa es un trastorno metab\u00f3lico que afecta la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar la glucosa como fuente de energ\u00eda."}{"title": "STATUS EPILEPTICUS:Status epilepticus is a serious medical condition characterized by prolonged or repeated seizures without recovery between them. It is considered a medical emergency due to the potential for significant complications. In cases where status epilepticus is refractory to standard treatments, the ketogenic diet may be utilized as a therapeutic option."}{"title": "CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS, or intensive care, refers to the specialized treatment provided to patients who are critically ill. This care is typically administered in intensive care units (ICUs), which are specialized medical facilities designed to offer comprehensive support to these patients. In ICUs, critically ill individuals receive close monitoring of vital signs, including glucose levels, and nutritional support tailored to their specific needs. Additionally, cuidados intensivos encompasses the management of severe medical conditions, such as status epilepticus, ensuring that patients receive the necessary interventions and therapies to stabilize their health."}{"title": "ANTICONVULSIVANTES:Los anticonvulsivantes son medicamentos utilizados para prevenir o tratar las crisis epil\u00e9pticas."}{"title": "CRISIS AT\u00d3NICAS:Las crisis at\u00f3nicas son episodios de p\u00e9rdida repentina del tono muscular, lo que puede llevar a ca\u00eddas o colapsos."}{"title": "CRISIS PARCIALES:Las crisis parciales son crisis epil\u00e9pticas que afectan solo una parte del cerebro y pueden manifestarse de diversas maneras, dependiendo de la regi\u00f3n afectada."}{"title": "CRISIS T\u00d3NICO-CL\u00d3NICAS GENERALIZADAS:Las crisis t\u00f3nico-cl\u00f3nicas generalizadas son un tipo de crisis epil\u00e9ptica que involucra contracciones musculares t\u00f3nicas seguidas de sacudidas cl\u00f3nicas, afectando todo el cuerpo."}{"title": "EPILEPSIA MIOCL\u00d3NICA SEVERA DE LA INFANCIA:La epilepsia miocl\u00f3nica severa de la infancia es un tipo de epilepsia que se presenta en la infancia y se caracteriza por convulsiones miocl\u00f3nicas frecuentes y severas."}{"title": "ACETAZOLAMIDA:Acetazolamida is a medication that is recommended to be taken on an empty stomach to enhance its absorption. It functions as a carbonic anhydrase inhibitor, which can lead to a significant risk of acidosis if used concurrently with a ketogenic diet."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO VALPROICO:El \u00e1cido valproico es un medicamento que inhibe la \u03b2-oxidaci\u00f3n y se conjuga con la carnitina acil-transferasa, lo que puede llevar a un d\u00e9ficit de carnitina."}{"title": "HIPERAMONIEMIA:La hiperamonemia es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica caracterizada por niveles elevados de amon\u00edaco en la sangre, que puede ser un efecto secundario en algunos pacientes."}{"title": "EDEMA CEREBRAL:Edema cerebral, or cerebral edema, is the swelling of the brain caused by an accumulation of excess fluid. This condition can arise in severe cases of hyponatremia and is considered a medical emergency that necessitates immediate intervention. Additionally, cerebral edema can be a complication in patients suffering from various metabolic conditions. The presence of excess fluid in the brain can lead to increased intracranial pressure and potentially serious health consequences, highlighting the importance of prompt diagnosis and treatment."}{"title": "CRISIS:Crisis refers to seizures experienced by patients with refractory epilepsy, characterized by episodes of abnormal electrical activity in the brain. The ketogenic diet is designed to reduce or eliminate these seizures in affected individuals. This dietary approach specifically targets the control of these episodes, aiming to improve the quality of life for patients suffering from epilepsy."}{"title": "ENSAYOS CL\u00cdNICOS ALEATORIZADOS:Los ensayos cl\u00ednicos aleatorizados son estudios que se utilizan para evaluar la eficacia de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica en comparaci\u00f3n con grupos de control."}{"title": "REVISI\u00d3N COCHRANE:La Revisi\u00f3n Cochrane es un an\u00e1lisis exhaustivo que incluye ensayos cl\u00ednicos sobre la eficacia de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica, proporcionando evidencia sobre su uso en pacientes. Adem\u00e1s, se trata de una revisi\u00f3n sistem\u00e1tica que eval\u00faa la efectividad de las f\u00f3rmulas inmunomoduladoras en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer. En conjunto, estas revisiones reflejan el compromiso de la Revisi\u00f3n Cochrane con la evaluaci\u00f3n rigurosa de intervenciones m\u00e9dicas y nutricionales, contribuyendo a la base de evidencia en el \u00e1mbito de la salud."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS Y ADOLESCENTES:Los ni\u00f1os y adolescentes son el grupo demogr\u00e1fico m\u00e1s estudiado en relaci\u00f3n con la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y su eficacia en la reducci\u00f3n de crisis epil\u00e9pticas."}{"title": "HIPOGLICEMIA HIPOCET\u00d3SICA:"}{"title": "DIETA ATKINS MODIFICADA:La Dieta Atkins Modificada es un enfoque diet\u00e9tico que se caracteriza por la limitaci\u00f3n de la ingesta de gl\u00facidos. Esta dieta ha sido objeto de varios estudios que eval\u00faan su eficacia en el tratamiento de crisis epil\u00e9pticas. Se considera una variante de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica, ya que tambi\u00e9n tiene como objetivo el control de las crisis, aunque se diferencia en las proporciones de macronutrientes que se utilizan."}{"title": "CUMPLIMIENTO:El cumplimiento es el grado en que los pacientes siguen las recomendaciones de la dieta, lo cual afecta la eficacia del tratamiento."}{"title": "EFICACIA:"}{"title": "MULTIVITAM\u00cdNICO:Un preparado multivitam\u00ednico con minerales y elementos traza es recomendado para evitar carencias en la dieta cetog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "EXCIPIENTES:Los excipientes de los medicamentos pueden influir en la efectividad de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica, siendo importante verificar su contenido."}{"title": "CONTROL AMBULATORIO:El control ambulatorio es necesario durante la realizaci\u00f3n de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica para asegurar un adecuado desarrollo pondoestatural y evitar complicaciones."}{"title": "JOHNS HOPKINS HOSPITAL:Johns Hopkins Hospital is a medical institution known for its research and treatment protocols, including the classic ketogenic diet for refractory epilepsy."}{"title": "DC:DC refers to a dietary treatment that has been extensively studied for its effects on various health parameters in children, particularly in relation to metabolic disorders and nutritional complications. Specifically, DC is recognized as the classic ketogenic diet, which has served as a standard treatment for refractory epilepsy for many years. This diet is commonly utilized for managing epileptic seizures and has been compared with other dietary approaches, such as the DAM, in several studies."}{"title": "DCSA:DCSA is a modified ketogenic diet without initial fasting, implemented gradually to achieve the desired caloric intake."}{"title": "DGSA:DGSA is a gradual ketogenic diet that progresses the ketogenic ratio from 1:1 to 4:1 over several days."}{"title": "VARIANTES DE DIETAS CETOG\u00c9NICAS:Variants of ketogenic diets include different types and modifications aimed at improving tolerability and effectiveness."}{"title": "HUTTENLOCHER:Huttenlocher is a researcher who initially described the medium-chain triglyceride (MCT) ketogenic diet in 1971."}{"title": "ATKINS DIET:The Atkins diet is a low-carbohydrate diet originally developed for weight loss. It has gained recognition as an alternative for individuals who may find the ketogenic diet too restrictive. In addition to its weight loss benefits, the Atkins diet has also been studied for its potential effectiveness in treating intractable epilepsy."}{"title": "MEDIUM-CHAIN TRIGLYCERIDES:Medium-chain triglycerides (MCTs) are a type of fat that can be used in ketogenic diets to enhance ketosis and improve palatability."}{"title": "CLASSIC KETOGENIC DIET:The classic ketogenic diet is a high-fat, low-carbohydrate diet that has been traditionally used to treat epilepsy."}{"title": "DIETARY PROTOCOL:Dietary protocols are structured plans for implementing specific diets, such as the gradual ketogenic diet protocol described in the text."}{"title": "COLLEGIATE STUDY:A collegiate study refers to research conducted in academic settings, often comparing different dietary approaches for medical conditions."}{"title": "DIETARY THERAPIES:"}{"title": "DAM:La DAM es un tratamiento diet\u00e9tico que se utiliza en combinaci\u00f3n con antiepil\u00e9pticos para reducir la frecuencia de crisis epil\u00e9pticas."}{"title": "LECHE CETOG\u00c9NICA:La Leche Cetog\u00e9nica es un complemento diet\u00e9tico que se utiliza en la dieta cetog\u00e9nica, especialmente para ni\u00f1os y pacientes con secuelas neurol\u00f3gicas."}{"title": "DIETA DE BAJO \u00cdNDICE GLUC\u00c9MICO:La Dieta de Bajo \u00cdndice Gluc\u00e9mico es una alternativa menos restrictiva a la DC y la DAM, permitiendo solo alimentos con un \u00edndice gluc\u00e9mico inferior a 50."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES METAB\u00d3LICAS:Las Complicaciones Metab\u00f3licas son efectos adversos que pueden surgir durante el tratamiento con dietas cetog\u00e9nicas, incluyendo deshidrataci\u00f3n y hipoglucemia."}{"title": "CRISIS EPIL\u00c9PTICAS:Las Crisis Epil\u00e9pticas son episodios de actividad el\u00e9ctrica anormal en el cerebro, que pueden ser tratados con dietas como la DAM y la DC."}{"title": "AYUNO INICIAL:El Ayuno Inicial es un protocolo que se utiliza en algunos tratamientos diet\u00e9ticos, que puede influir en la aparici\u00f3n de complicaciones como la deshidrataci\u00f3n."}{"title": "SUEROTERAPIA DE MANTENIMIENTO:La Sueroterapia de Mantenimiento es un tratamiento que se utiliza para prevenir la deshidrataci\u00f3n en pacientes que siguen dietas cetog\u00e9nicas."}{"title": "ESTUDIOS ALEATORIZADOS:"}{"title": "HIPOGLUCEMIA GRAVE:Grave hipo glucemia refers to severe and prolonged low blood sugar levels that can occur as a complication of metabolic disorders."}{"title": "HYPERCOLESTEROLIEMIA:Hypercolesterolemia is a condition of elevated cholesterol levels in the blood, frequently observed in patients."}{"title": "HYPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA:Hypertrigliceridemia is a condition characterized by high triglyceride levels in the blood, which has been noted in a significant percentage of patients."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES DIGESTIVAS:Las complicaciones digestivas son efectos secundarios comunes de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica, incluyendo diarrea, n\u00e1useas y v\u00f3mitos."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES CARD\u00cdACAS:Las complicaciones card\u00edacas, aunque raras, pueden incluir miocardiopat\u00eda y trastornos del ritmo en pacientes en dieta cetog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "CRECIMIENTO LINEAL:El crecimiento lineal en ni\u00f1os tratados con dieta cetog\u00e9nica puede verse afectado, especialmente con una proporci\u00f3n proteica inadecuada."}{"title": "ESTUDIO DE 6 MESES:Un estudio que evalu\u00f3 la evoluci\u00f3n pondoestatural de ni\u00f1os tratados con dieta cetog\u00e9nica durante 6 meses."}{"title": "ESTUDIO DE 15 MESES:Un estudio que compar\u00f3 el gasto energ\u00e9tico y el crecimiento en ni\u00f1os con dieta cetog\u00e9nica y ni\u00f1os sanos durante 15 meses."}{"title": "ESTUDIO RETROSPECTIVO:\"ESTUDIO RETROSPECTIVO\" se refiere a un an\u00e1lisis que examina diferentes aspectos relacionados con la dieta cetog\u00e9nica. Este estudio sugiere que el retraso en el crecimiento en ni\u00f1os que siguen una dieta cetog\u00e9nica podr\u00eda estar vinculado al aporte proteico que reciben. Adem\u00e1s, el estudio retrospectivo ha encontrado que el uso de citrato pot\u00e1sico est\u00e1 asociado con una menor prevalencia de litiasis renal en pacientes que son tratados con esta misma dieta. En conjunto, estos hallazgos destacan tanto las preocupaciones sobre el crecimiento infantil como los beneficios potenciales en la prevenci\u00f3n de problemas renales en el contexto de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "N\u00c1USEAS Y V\u00d3MITOS:N\u00e1useas y v\u00f3mitos are gastrointestinal symptoms that can arise from the sudden onset of the ketogenic diet, particularly related to the degree of ketosis experienced by individuals."}{"title": "FIBROGASTROSCOPIA:Fibrogastroscopia is a medical procedure utilized to evaluate gastrointestinal health, particularly in patients preparing to begin a ketogenic diet. This procedure enables doctors to visualize the upper digestive tract, which includes the esophagus, stomach, and duodenum. It is instrumental in diagnosing various conditions that may affect these areas, ensuring that any underlying issues are identified and addressed before the initiation of dietary changes."}{"title": "MIOCARDIOPAT\u00cdA:Miocardiopat\u00eda is a rare cardiac complication associated with selenium deficiency in patients on a ketogenic diet."}{"title": "PROLONGACI\u00d3N DEL INTERVALO QT:Prolongaci\u00f3n del intervalo QT is a cardiac rhythm disorder observed in some children on a ketogenic diet."}{"title": "DESMINERALIZACI\u00d3N \u00d3SEA:Desmineralizaci\u00f3n \u00f3sea is a risk for patients on a ketogenic diet due to chronic acidosis, leading to potential osteopenia."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N CON CALCIO Y VITAMINA D:Suplementaci\u00f3n con calcio y vitamina D is recommended for patients on a ketogenic diet to prevent bone demineralization."}{"title": "BAILEY EE:Bailey EE es un autor que ha investigado el uso de la dieta en el tratamiento de la epilepsia, contribuyendo a la literatura m\u00e9dica sobre el tema."}{"title": "PFEIFER HH:Pfeifer HH es un autor que ha colaborado en estudios sobre la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y su eficacia en el tratamiento de la epilepsia."}{"title": "THIELE EA:Thiele EA es un autor que ha investigado el uso de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica en el tratamiento de la epilepsia, aportando a la comprensi\u00f3n de su eficacia."}{"title": "MARTIN K:Martin K es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci\u00f3n sobre la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y otros tratamientos diet\u00e9ticos para la epilepsia."}{"title": "JACKSON CF:Jackson CF es un autor que ha colaborado en estudios sobre la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y su efectividad en el tratamiento de la epilepsia."}{"title": "LEVY RG:Levy RG es un autor que ha investigado la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y su uso en el tratamiento de la epilepsia, contribuyendo a la literatura m\u00e9dica."}{"title": "COOPER PN:Cooper PN es un autor que ha trabajado en la investigaci\u00f3n sobre la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y otros tratamientos diet\u00e9ticos para la epilepsia."}{"title": "KOSSOFF EH:Kossoff E. H. is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his extensive work on the ketogenic diet and its application in treating epilepsy. He has conducted significant studies that explore the efficacy of dietary therapies, particularly the ketogenic diet, in managing this neurological condition. His contributions to the field have been influential in advancing the understanding of how dietary interventions can benefit individuals with epilepsy."}{"title": "ZUPEC-KANIA B:Zupec-Kania B es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci\u00f3n sobre la dieta cetog\u00e9nica y su aplicaci\u00f3n en el tratamiento de la epilepsia."}{"title": "ADHERENCIA A LA DIETA:La buena adherencia a la dieta cetog\u00e9nica es un factor determinante en su efectividad para el tratamiento de la epilepsia."}{"title": "VIGILANCIA DE GLUCEMIA:La vigilancia de la glucemia es crucial durante la instauraci\u00f3n de la dieta cetog\u00e9nica para asegurar la salud del paciente."}{"title": "VIGILANCIA DE HIDRATACI\u00d3N:La vigilancia del estado de hidrataci\u00f3n es importante durante el seguimiento de pacientes en la dieta cetog\u00e9nica para prevenir complicaciones."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N CON VITAMINAS Y MINERALES:La suplementaci\u00f3n con vitaminas y minerales es recomendada para cubrir los requerimientos de los pacientes en la dieta cetog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "MIOCARDIOPAT\u00cdA POR D\u00c9FICIT DE SELENIO:La miocardiopat\u00eda por d\u00e9ficit de selenio es una complicaci\u00f3n potencialmente fatal que puede ocurrir en pacientes en la dieta cetog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "PEDIATRICS:Pediatrics is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to the health and medical care of infants, children, and adolescents. It publishes a wide range of research and reviews focused on child health, including studies on various topics such as vitamin K status in children with cystic fibrosis and the impact of iron deficiency on cognitive achievement among school-aged children. The journal also provides guidelines for the diagnosis and prevention of iron deficiency in infants and young children, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in pediatric health. Overall, Pediatrics serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge and practices related to the health and well-being of children."}{"title": "NORDLI:D. Nordli is a researcher and author who has contributed to the understanding and application of the ketogenic diet in treating epilepsy."}{"title": "FREEMAN:J.M. Freeman is a medical professional known for his work on the ketogenic diet and its efficacy in treating seizure disorders."}{"title": "KINSMA:S.L. Kinsman is a researcher who has studied the efficacy of the ketogenic diet for intractable seizure disorders."}{"title": "KLEPPER:J. Klepper is a researcher who has investigated the effects of the ketogenic diet in various medical conditions, including GLUT1 deficiency syndrome."}{"title": "KOREAN MULTICENTRIC EXPERIENCE:The Korean multicentric experience refers to a study conducted across multiple centers in Korea evaluating the efficacy and safety of the ketogenic diet for intractable childhood epilepsy."}{"title": "SEIZURE DISORDERS:Seizure disorders encompass a range of conditions characterized by recurrent seizures, often treated with various interventions, including the ketogenic diet."}{"title": "GLUT1 DEFICIENCY SYNDROME:"}{"title": "J CHILD NEUROL:Journal of Child Neurology publishes research on neurological disorders in children, including studies on the ketogenic diet."}{"title": "LANCET NEUROL:Lancet Neurology is a medical journal that publishes research on neurological conditions, including epilepsy."}{"title": "EPILEPSY BEHAV:Epilepsy & Behavior is a journal that focuses on the behavioral aspects of epilepsy and its treatment."}{"title": "J CLIN NEUROL:Journal of Clinical Neurology publishes clinical research on neurological disorders, including studies on the ketogenic diet."}{"title": "EPILEPSY RES:Epilepsy Research is a journal that publishes research on epilepsy and its treatment options."}{"title": "NEAL EG:Neal E. G. is a researcher actively engaged in multiple studies and clinical trials that evaluate the efficacy of the ketogenic diet for the treatment of epilepsy. His work focuses on comparing different variations of the ketogenic diet to determine their effectiveness in managing this condition."}{"title": "FREEMAN JM:Freeman J. M. is a researcher who has published extensively on the ketogenic diet and its effects on seizure disorders."}{"title": "RATIOS:The study of different lipid:nonlipid ratios in ketogenic diets to evaluate their efficacy and tolerability in epilepsy treatment."}{"title": "MARTINEZ CC:Martinez C. C. is a researcher involved in studies on the ketogenic diet and its effects on seizure disorders."}{"title": "SEO JH:Seo J. H. is a researcher who has studied the efficacy and tolerability of the ketogenic diet in epilepsy treatment."}{"title": "RAJU KNV:Raju K. N. V. is a researcher who has conducted studies comparing different ketogenic diet ratios in treating refractory epilepsy."}{"title": "FUEHRLEIN BS:Fuehrlein B. S. is a researcher who has explored the metabolic effects of ketogenic diets in epilepsy treatment."}{"title": "TALLIAN KB:Tallian K. B. is a researcher who has studied the role of the ketogenic diet in children with intractable seizures."}{"title": "VAN DER LOUW EJTM:Van Der Louw E. J. T. M. is a researcher who has investigated the effects of concomitant lamotrigine use on the ketogenic diet's efficacy."}{"title": "HENDERSON CB:"}{"title": "EPILEPSY RESEARCH:Epilepsy Research is a journal that publishes studies related to epilepsy, including dietary interventions like the ketogenic diet."}{"title": "BRAIN DEVELOPMENT:Brain Development is a journal that publishes research on neurological development, including studies on dietary impacts on childhood epilepsy."}{"title": "PEDIATRIC NEUROLOGY:Pediatric Neurology is a journal that focuses on neurological disorders in children, including epilepsy and dietary treatments."}{"title": "SEIZURE:Seizure is a journal that publishes research on seizure disorders, including the effects of dietary interventions."}{"title": "REIF PS:Reif PS is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the ketogenic diet for epilepsy management."}{"title": "BAUER S:Bauer S is a researcher who has worked on the ketogenic diet and its application in treating epilepsy."}{"title": "BELKE M:Belke M is a researcher involved in the study of the ketogenic diet for epilepsy treatment."}{"title": "OERTEL WH:Oertel WH is a researcher who has studied the ketogenic diet's effects on epilepsy."}{"title": "KNAKE S:Knake S is a researcher who has contributed to research on the ketogenic diet and epilepsy."}{"title": "HUTTENLOCHER PR:Huttenlocher PR is a researcher known for studies on the ketogenic diet and its metabolic effects in epilepsy."}{"title": "KAPETANAKIS M:Kapetanakis M is a researcher who has studied the effects of the ketogenic diet on vascular function in epilepsy patients."}{"title": "LIUBA P:Liuba P is a researcher involved in studies on the ketogenic diet and its effects on epilepsy."}{"title": "ODERMARSKY M:Odermarsky M is a researcher who has contributed to research on the ketogenic diet for epilepsy treatment."}{"title": "HALLB\u00d6\u00d6K T:Hallb\u00f6\u00f6k T is a researcher who has studied the effects of the ketogenic diet on children with epilepsy."}{"title": "STRZELCZYK A:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL SAN JORGE:Hospital San Jorge is a medical facility located in Huesca, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL DE LA DEFENSA:Hospital General de la Defensa is a hospital in Zaragoza, serving as a chief service for endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "AMAYA BARRAG\u00c1N ANGULO:Amaya Barrag\u00e1n Angulo is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Unit at Hospital San Jorge."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA LUISA GRACIA RUIZ:Mar\u00eda Luisa Gracia Ruiz is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet."}{"title": "VICENTE BLAY CORT\u00c9S:Vicente Blay Cort\u00e9s is the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital General de la Defensa."}{"title": "COREA:Corea es un pa\u00eds asi\u00e1tico que recomienda un consumo de sodio de 2 g/d\u00eda y de sal de 5 g/d\u00eda."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA CONGESTIVA:Insuficiencia card\u00edaca congestiva, tambi\u00e9n conocida como congestive heart failure, es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson, una afecci\u00f3n caracterizada por la acumulaci\u00f3n de cobre en el organismo que afecta el coraz\u00f3n. Esta enfermedad se manifiesta con s\u00edntomas como edemas y requiere una restricci\u00f3n diet\u00e9tica de sodio para mejorar la funci\u00f3n card\u00edaca."}{"title": "GU\u00cdAS AMERICANAS Y CANADIENSES:Las gu\u00edas americanas y canadienses recomiendan un consumo de sodio de 1,5 g/d\u00eda y de sal de 3,8 g/d\u00eda."}{"title": "AM\u00c9RICA:"}{"title": "EDEMA C\u00cdCLICO IDIOP\u00c1TICO:El edema c\u00edclico idiop\u00e1tico es un s\u00edndrome que afecta principalmente a mujeres, caracterizado por episodios de edema y distensi\u00f3n abdominal."}{"title": "DIETA CONTROLADA EN SODIO:The \"DIETA CONTROLADA EN SODIO\" refers to a dietary regimen that restricts sodium intake to help manage fluid balance and blood pressure, particularly in patients with renal issues. This controlled sodium diet is essential for individuals dealing with hypertension and other related health problems, as it aids in maintaining overall health and preventing complications associated with excessive sodium consumption."}{"title": "INTERSALT:The INTERSALT study is a significant research initiative that investigates the relationship between sodium consumption and blood pressure. Published in 1988, the study found a clear correlation between sodium intake and blood pressure levels, concluding that a daily sodium intake of 6 grams could lead to reductions in both systolic and diastolic blood pressure. This influential study has contributed to the understanding of how dietary sodium affects cardiovascular health."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS ENLATADOS:Los alimentos enlatados son productos que a menudo contienen sodio como conservante."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS PRECOCINADOS:Los alimentos precocinados son productos que suelen contener sodio para su conservaci\u00f3n y sabor."}{"title": "ETIQUETADO DE ALIMENTOS:El etiquetado de alimentos es un proceso que informa sobre el contenido de sodio y otros nutrientes en los productos alimenticios."}{"title": "CARNES SALADAS:Refers to salted or cured meats that are discouraged in a low-sodium diet."}{"title": "PESCADOS SALADOS:Refers to salted fish products that are discouraged in a low-sodium diet."}{"title": "QUESOS CURADOS:Refers to aged cheeses that are high in sodium and discouraged in a low-sodium diet."}{"title": "AGUA MINERAL CON GAS:Refers to carbonated mineral water that may contain sodium and is discouraged in a low-sodium diet."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS DESACONSEJADOS:"}{"title": "DIETA HIPOS\u00d3DICA MODERADA:Ejemplo de dieta hipos\u00f3dica moderada para una persona de 70 a\u00f1os y 70 kg, que incluye varias comidas y alimentos espec\u00edficos para controlar el sodio."}{"title": "DIETA HIPOS\u00d3DICA ESTRICTA:Ejemplo de dieta hipos\u00f3dica estricta para un adulto de 70 kg de peso, que detalla comidas y alimentos con bajo contenido de sodio."}{"title": "VINAGRE:El vinagre es un potenciador del sabor recomendado para la cocina sin sal."}{"title": "HIERBAS AROM\u00c1TICAS:Las hierbas arom\u00e1ticas son recomendadas para potenciar el sabor de los alimentos en una dieta sin sal."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN SODIO:Los alimentos ricos en sodio deben ser evitados en una dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "CASTA\u00d1A:La casta\u00f1a es un tipo de fruto seco que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "AVELLANA:La avellana es un tipo de fruto seco que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "COCO DESSECADO:El coco desecado es un tipo de fruta que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "D\u00c1TIL SECO:El d\u00e1til seco es un tipo de fruta que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "MELOCOT\u00d3N SECO:El melocot\u00f3n seco es un tipo de fruta que se menciona como parte de los alimentos recomendados en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "ALB\u00d3NDIGAS:Las alb\u00f3ndigas son un tipo de alimento que se menciona en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica moderada."}{"title": "PAN SIN SAL:El pan sin sal es un tipo de pan recomendado en las dietas hipos\u00f3dicas."}{"title": "SOPA:SOPA, or soup, is a type of food that plays a significant role in a strict low-sodium diet. It is recognized for its benefits in hydration and nutrition, particularly during episodes of diarrhea, making it a valuable option for maintaining health in such situations."}{"title": "POLLO ASADO:El pollo asado es un tipo de alimento que se menciona en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica estricta."}{"title": "ENSALADA:La ensalada es un tipo de comida que se menciona en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica estricta."}{"title": "CROQUETAS DE PESCADO:Las croquetas de pescado son un tipo de alimento que se menciona en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica estricta."}{"title": "REQUES\u00d3N:El reques\u00f3n es un tipo de queso que se menciona en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica estricta."}{"title": "PAPILLOTE:M\u00e9todo de cocci\u00f3n que se recomienda para preparar alimentos en una dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "ESTOFADOS:M\u00e9todo de cocci\u00f3n que se recomienda para preparar alimentos en una dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "GUISADOS:M\u00e9todo de cocci\u00f3n que se recomienda para preparar alimentos en una dieta hipos\u00f3dica."}{"title": "CUIDADO DEL SODIO:El cuidado del sodio es un aspecto importante en la dieta hipos\u00f3dica, que implica evitar alimentos ricos en sodio."}{"title": "ALMENDRA TOSTADA:"}{"title": "DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO:The \"DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO\" refers to a potassium-controlled diet specifically designed to limit potassium intake. This dietary regimen is particularly important for managing conditions such as hyperkalemia, especially in patients with renal issues. Additionally, the diet plays a crucial role in regulating potassium levels, which is vital for maintaining cardiovascular and muscular health. By controlling potassium intake, individuals can better manage their health conditions and promote overall well-being."}{"title": "DI\u00c1LISIS PERITONEAL CONTINUA:Continuous peritoneal dialysis is a treatment that allows for a lower risk of hyperkalemia due to constant therapy."}{"title": "HYPERKALIEMIA:"}{"title": "ALIMENTOS INTEGRALES:Alimentos integrales are whole foods that are generally high in potassium and phosphorus, which should be avoided by patients on a restricted diet."}{"title": "PACIENTES EN DI\u00c1LISIS:Patients undergoing dialysis who require specific dietary management to maintain their health and prevent complications related to kidney failure."}{"title": "HIPERCALIEMIA:Hipercaliemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated potassium levels in the blood, which can occur in patients with renal failure."}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN POTASIO:A diet that provides at least 100-175 mEq of potassium per day, used for managing and preventing hypokalemia."}{"title": "SISTEMA SCORE:A method developed by European societies for calculating total cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "ESTUDIO FRAMINGHAM:A study that observed the prevalence of hypertension in obese individuals compared to those with normal weight."}{"title": "NATRIURESIS:The process of sodium excretion in the urine, which can be influenced by potassium intake."}{"title": "HYPERTENSI\u00d3N:A general term for high blood pressure, which includes various forms such as essential and secondary hypertension."}{"title": "PATHS:The PATHS study investigates the effects of alcohol consumption reduction on blood pressure, providing insights into hypertension management."}{"title": "NATIONAL HIGH BLOOD PRESSURE EDUCATION PROGRAM:The National High Blood Pressure Education Program is an initiative designed to educate both the public and healthcare professionals about hypertension, its prevention, and treatment. The program focuses on raising awareness regarding high blood pressure and aims to provide valuable information to help individuals manage and prevent this common health issue."}{"title": "NATIONAL HEART, LUNG AND BLOOD INSTITUTE:The National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) conducts research and provides information on heart, lung, and blood diseases, including hypertension."}{"title": "PA:PA can refer to two distinct medical concepts: blood pressure and pancreatitis. In the context of blood pressure, PA (Presi\u00f3n Arterial) is a critical factor in diagnosing and managing hypertension, which is essential for maintaining cardiovascular health. On the other hand, PA also denotes pancreatitis, a condition characterized by inflammation of the pancreas that can result in various metabolic disturbances. This condition necessitates careful nutritional support to manage its effects and promote recovery. Thus, PA encompasses both the important measurement of blood pressure and the medical condition of pancreatitis, each with its own implications for health management."}{"title": "ESTUDIO DASH-SODIO:The DASH-sodium study focused on reducing sodium intake in various diets to observe its effects on blood pressure levels."}{"title": "STAMLER:Stamler is a researcher who published findings in 1992 regarding the prevalence of hypertension in primitive societies compared to industrialized ones."}{"title": "CARNES, AVES Y PESCADOS:Carnes, aves y pescados are sources of protein and magnesium, including lean meats and fish."}{"title": "LEGUMBRES Y FRUTOS SECOS:Legumbres y frutos secos are sources of energy, magnesium, potassium, protein, and fiber, including nuts and seeds."}{"title": "JOINT NATIONAL COMMITTEE:The Joint National Committee is a collective that focuses on establishing guidelines for the prevention, detection, evaluation, and treatment of high blood pressure, also known as hypertension. This committee offers comprehensive recommendations for managing hypertension, which include considerations for dietary sodium and potassium intake, among other factors."}{"title": "HTA RESISTENTE A LA SAL:HTA resistente a la sal se refiere a las personas que no experimentan un aumento en la presi\u00f3n arterial con el consumo de sal."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD CORONARIA:La mortalidad coronaria se refiere a las muertes causadas por enfermedades del coraz\u00f3n, que pueden verse afectadas por la ingesta de sodio."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD POR ICTUS:La mortalidad por ictus se refiere a las muertes causadas por accidentes cerebrovasculares, que pueden estar influenciadas por la presi\u00f3n arterial y la ingesta de sodio."}{"title": "DIETA VEGETARIANA:A vegetarian diet is typically rich in polyunsaturated fatty acids and low in saturated fats, which may contribute to lower blood pressure."}{"title": "ACEITES INSATURADOS:Unsaturated oils are fats that can influence blood pressure and are often recommended for a healthy diet."}{"title": "KOREAN NUTRITION SOCIETY:The Korean Nutrition Society is an organization that provides dietary reference intakes and nutritional guidelines for the Korean population."}{"title": "JAPANESE SOCIETY OF HYPERTENSION:The Japanese Society of Hypertension is a professional organization focused on research and guidelines related to hypertension and cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "TABLAS DE ALIMENTOS:Food tables classify foods into recommended and discouraged categories for patients requiring sodium-controlled diets."}{"title": "EXERCISE F\u00cdSICO:"}{"title": "HFSA:Heart Failure Society of America, an organization that provides guidelines for heart failure management"}{"title": "SODIUM-HF:A pilot study investigating the long-term effects of dietary sodium restriction on clinical outcomes in heart failure patients"}{"title": "AM HEART J:AM HEART J, or the American Heart Journal, is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research focused on cardiovascular health. It serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings in the field of cardiology. Notably, in 2003, the journal published a study examining the effects of furosemide and hypertonic saline in the context of heart failure, contributing valuable insights to the understanding and treatment of this condition."}{"title": "BEST PRACT RES CLIN ENDOCRINOL METAB:Best Practice & Research Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism, a journal focusing on endocrinology and metabolism"}{"title": "MIDDLE EAST J DIG DIS:Middle East Journal of Digestive Diseases, a publication that discusses issues related to digestive health"}{"title": "SEMIN DIAL:Seminars in Dialysis, a journal that covers topics related to dialysis and kidney health"}{"title": "WORLD HEALTH ORGANISATION:The World Health Organization, a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for international public health"}{"title": "MCMAHON EJ:McMahon EJ is a researcher who has contributed to studies on dietary salt intake for chronic kidney disease patients"}{"title": "NIELS A:Niels A is a researcher who has studied the effects of sodium restriction on various health parameters"}{"title": "LINDLEY EJ:"}{"title": "EUROPEAN PROSPECTIVE INVESTIGATION INTO CANCER AND NUTRITION:A large-scale study investigating the relationship between diet, nutrition, and cancer across multiple countries in Europe."}{"title": "KAMYAR KALANTAR-ZADEH:A researcher involved in studies related to dietary restrictions in dialysis patients and their nutritional needs."}{"title": "SEMINARS IN DIALYSIS:A journal that focuses on the management and treatment of patients undergoing dialysis, including dietary considerations."}{"title": "EUROPEAN HEART JOURNAL:A leading journal in cardiovascular medicine that publishes guidelines and research related to heart health."}{"title": "AGNOLI C:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "ERICSON U:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "JOHANSSON I:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "FERRARI P:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "ENGESET D:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "LUND E:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "LENTJES M:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "KEY T:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "TOUVIER M:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "NIRAVONG M:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "LARRA\u00d1AGA N:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "RODR\u00cdGUEZ L:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "OCK\u00c9 MC:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "PEETERS PH:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "TJ\u00d8NNELAND A:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "BJERREGAARD L:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "VASILOPOULOU E:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "DILIS V:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "LINSEISEN J:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "N\u00d6THLINGS U:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "RIBOLI E:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "SLIMANI N:A researcher involved in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study focusing on dietary intake."}{"title": "BINGHAM S:A researcher contributing to the study of dietary intake variations in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study."}{"title": "TUMINO R:"}{"title": "SCORE PROJECT:The SCORE project is a research initiative focused on estimating the ten-year risk of fatal cardiovascular disease in Europe."}{"title": "DASH COLLABORATIVE RESEARCH GROUP:The DASH Collaborative Research Group is a dedicated team that conducts clinical trials aimed at studying the effects of dietary patterns on blood pressure. Their research focuses on understanding how different dietary approaches can influence blood pressure levels, contributing valuable insights to the field of nutrition and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "INTERSALT STUDY:The INTERSALT Study is a research study that investigates the relationship between sodium intake and blood pressure across different populations."}{"title": "US:The United States is a country where several studies on hypertension and dietary factors have been conducted."}{"title": "WANG RS:Wang RS is a co-author of a study on ambulatory systolic blood pressure in hypertensive smokers."}{"title": "ASCHERIO A:Ascherio A is a researcher involved in a prospective study of nutritional factors and hypertension among US men."}{"title": "GIOVANNUCCI EL:Giovannucci EL is a researcher who contributed to a study on nutritional factors and hypertension among US men."}{"title": "WITTMAN JC:Witteman JC is a researcher who studied nutritional factors and hypertension among US women."}{"title": "SACKS FM:Sacks FM is a researcher involved in studies related to hypertension and dietary factors."}{"title": "HE J:He J is a researcher who studied the long-term effects of weight loss and dietary sodium reduction on hypertension incidence."}{"title": "WHELTON P:Whelton P is a researcher who has contributed to studies on hypertension and dietary factors."}{"title": "CUSHMAN WC:Cushman WC is a researcher involved in the Prevention and Treatment of Hypertension Study (PATHS)."}{"title": "FENG J:Feng J is a researcher who studied plasma sodium and its effects on hypertension."}{"title": "TRIALS OF HYPERTENSION PREVENTION COLLABORATIVE RESEARCH GROUP:The Trials of Hypertension Prevention Collaborative Research Group is a dedicated research entity focused on investigating interventions aimed at preventing hypertension. This group conducts comprehensive studies to evaluate the impact of lifestyle changes on the development and management of hypertension, contributing valuable insights into effective prevention strategies."}{"title": "MANN SJ:"}{"title": "ANA ISABEL ILUNDAIN GONZ\u00c1LEZ:Ana Isabel Ilundain Gonz\u00e1lez is a medical professional affiliated with the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa, where she specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. She is also a co-author engaged in research related to nephrolithiasis and dietary management, contributing to the understanding of how diet impacts kidney stone formation and overall health."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA JULIA OC\u00d3N BRET\u00d3N:Mar\u00eda Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n is a medical professional affiliated with the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa, where she specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical work, she is also an author and researcher, with a particular focus on nephrolithiasis and dietary treatments. Her expertise encompasses both the medical and research aspects of her fields, contributing to advancements in understanding and managing conditions related to nutrition and kidney health."}{"title": "JOS\u00c9 ANTONIO GIMENO ORNA:Jos\u00e9 Antonio Gimeno Orna is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa, focusing on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "JORDI PONS DOLSET:Jordi Pons Dolset is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Royo Villanova, focusing on rheumatology."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF PREVENTIVE CARDIOLOGY:The European Journal of Preventive Cardiology is a journal that publishes research on cardiovascular health and prevention strategies."}{"title": "HORMONAS CALCITROPAS:Las hormonas calciotropas son un grupo de tres hormonas que regulan el metabolismo del calcio en el cuerpo, actuando en el intestino, ri\u00f1\u00f3n y hueso."}{"title": "GL\u00c1NDULAS PARATIROIDES:Las gl\u00e1ndulas paratiroides son gl\u00e1ndulas endocrinas que regulan los niveles de calcio en la sangre mediante la secreci\u00f3n de hormona paratiroidea."}{"title": "ALCALOSIS METAB\u00d3LICA:La alcalosis metab\u00f3lica es un trastorno que tambi\u00e9n puede aumentar la fijaci\u00f3n del calcio a la alb\u00famina, afectando los niveles de calcio ionizado."}{"title": "CALCIO PLASM\u00c1TICO:"}{"title": "FGF-23:El FGF-23 es una hormona producida por los osteocitos que tiene un efecto fosfat\u00farico potente, disminuyendo la absorci\u00f3n intestinal de f\u00f3sforo."}{"title": "DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO:A controlled calcium diet, known as \"DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO,\" is an approach that emphasizes the regulation of calcium intake to prevent and treat conditions such as osteoporosis and hypercalcemia. This dietary strategy focuses on achieving a balanced nutrient intake, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary amounts of calcium while managing their overall health. By carefully monitoring calcium consumption, this diet aims to support bone health and prevent complications associated with excessive calcium levels."}{"title": "ALUMINIO:Aluminio is a chemical element that serves as a component in certain antacids. It has been noted for its ability to inhibit gastric motility, which can lead to gastrointestinal complications, particularly when combined with enteral nutrition. Additionally, aluminum is associated with toxicity in parenteral nutrition, which can adversely affect bone mass. The element is linked to various medical conditions and poses a risk of intoxication, highlighting the need for caution in its use within medical treatments."}{"title": "TIAZIDAS:TIAZIDAS, or thiazides, are a class of diuretics that play a significant role in influencing the levels of calcium and phosphorus in the body. These medications are known for their ability to retain calcium, which can have various effects on the body's mineral balance."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZADOS:The term \"HOSPITALIZADOS\" refers to hospitalized patients, who are individuals receiving medical care in a hospital setting. These patients often require nutritional support during their stay to aid in their recovery and overall health management."}{"title": "PACIENTES S\u00c9PTICOS:Patients who are septic are also at increased risk for developing hypophosphatemia."}{"title": "CALCIFICACIONES DE TEJIDOS BLANDOS:Soft tissue calcifications are complications that can arise from prolonged elevated phosphorus levels in patients with chronic kidney disease.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "HUESO:HUESO, which translates to \"bone\" in English, serves as a major storage site for magnesium in the body, containing approximately 60% of the total body magnesium."}{"title": "CARBONATO DE LANTANO:Lanthanum carbonate is a medication used to reduce phosphate levels in patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "PTH INTACTA:Intact parathyroid hormone (PTH) is a hormone that regulates calcium and magnesium levels in the body."}{"title": "SEVELAMER:"}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE WHIPPLE:La enfermedad de Whipple es una enfermedad infecciosa que afecta la absorci\u00f3n intestinal, lo que puede llevar a deficiencias de magnesio."}{"title": "F\u00c1RMACOS INHIBIDORES DE LA BOMBA DE PROTONES:Los f\u00e1rmacos inhibidores de la bomba de protones son medicamentos que reducen la producci\u00f3n de \u00e1cido en el est\u00f3mago y pueden contribuir a la malabsorci\u00f3n de magnesio."}{"title": "RESORCI\u00d3N \u00d3SEA:La resorci\u00f3n \u00f3sea es el proceso por el cual el tejido \u00f3seo es descompuesto, lo que puede aumentar el riesgo de osteoporosis."}{"title": "FORMACI\u00d3N \u00d3SEA:La formaci\u00f3n \u00f3sea es el proceso de creaci\u00f3n de nuevo tejido \u00f3seo, que se ve afectado por factores hormonales y nutricionales."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA:PROTE\u00cdNA is a macronutrient that plays a crucial role in healing and immune response, making it particularly important in the nutritional management of critically ill patients. However, an excessive intake of protein in the diet can disrupt the balance of electrolytes, including magnesium, potentially leading to a condition known as hypomagnesemia. This highlights the importance of maintaining a balanced protein intake to support health while avoiding negative effects on electrolyte levels."}{"title": "FRAX:Fracture Risk Assessment Tool (FRAX) is a computer tool used to evaluate the risk of fractures in patients, calculating the probability of suffering a fracture within ten years."}{"title": "VITAMIN K:Vitamin K is a fat-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in blood clotting and bone health. It is essential for the proper functioning of various proteins involved in these processes, particularly in the mineralization of the organic matrix of collagen in bones. Vitamin K is often monitored in patients with specific conditions, such as those with FQ (fluoroquinolone) and EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease), as it has particular recommendations for these individuals. Overall, Vitamin K is vital for maintaining both blood coagulation and bone metabolism."}{"title": "TOBACCO:Tobacco is an independent risk factor for fractures, accelerating bone mass loss, especially in women."}{"title": "CAFFEINE:Caffeine can increase urinary calcium excretion, which may affect calcium balance in elderly individuals or postmenopausal women."}{"title": "SEDENTARISM:Sedentarism is a lifestyle factor that can increase the risk of developing osteoporosis."}{"title": "SMOKING:Smoking is a lifestyle factor that contributes to the risk of osteoporosis."}{"title": "DIETARY IMBALANCE:Dietary imbalance, including low calcium intake, is a significant risk factor for osteoporosis."}{"title": "ANTIANDROGENS:Antiandrogens are medications that may increase the risk of osteoporosis."}{"title": "THYROXINE:Excessive doses of thyroxine can lead to osteoporosis."}{"title": "ANTICONVULSANTS:Certain anticonvulsants are associated with an increased risk of osteoporosis."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOPATHIES:Endocrinopathies such as hyperthyroidism and Cushing's disease can contribute to the risk of osteoporosis."}{"title": "MALABSORPTIVE DISEASES:Malabsorptive diseases can lead to osteoporosis due to inadequate nutrient absorption."}{"title": "RENAL DISEASES:Renal diseases can affect bone health and contribute to osteoporosis."}åù0␀␀␀␀␀û0␀␀␀␀␀Ωü0␀␀␀␀␀`†0␀␀␀␀␀˚†0␀␀␀␀␀ù°0␀␀␀␀␀π°0␀␀␀␀␀t¢0␀␀␀␀␀˝¢0␀␀␀␀␀~¶0␀␀␀␀␀␀®0␀␀␀␀␀Q©0␀␀␀␀␀à™0␀␀␀␀␀¨0␀␀␀␀␀≥≠0␀␀␀␀␀8Æ0␀␀␀␀␀≈Æ0␀␀␀␀␀ﬂÆ0␀␀␀␀␀ôØ0␀␀␀␀␀$≤0␀␀␀␀␀Ó≤0␀␀␀␀␀©≥0␀␀␀␀␀b¥0␀␀␀␀␀2∂0␀␀␀␀␀∑0␀␀␀␀␀∂∑0␀␀␀␀␀ƒ∫0␀␀␀␀␀8ª0␀␀␀␀␀§ª0␀␀␀␀␀™º0␀␀␀␀␀.Ω0␀␀␀␀␀…Ω0␀␀␀␀␀aæ0␀␀␀␀␀˚æ0␀␀␀␀␀®ø0␀␀␀␀␀C¿0␀␀␀␀␀–¿0␀␀␀␀␀ä¡0␀␀␀␀␀¬0␀␀␀␀␀x√0␀␀␀␀␀Éƒ0␀␀␀␀␀;≈0␀␀␀␀␀∆0␀␀␀␀␀…∆0␀␀␀␀␀È«0␀␀␀␀␀K…0␀␀␀␀␀t…0␀␀␀␀␀…0␀␀␀␀␀l 0␀␀␀␀␀`Õ0␀␀␀␀␀–0␀␀␀␀␀™–0␀␀␀␀␀@—0␀␀␀␀␀”0␀␀␀␀␀ù”0␀␀␀␀␀.‘0␀␀␀␀␀ã’0␀␀␀␀␀b÷0␀␀␀␀␀◊0␀␀␀␀␀£◊0␀␀␀␀␀lÿ0␀␀␀␀␀†ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀YŸ0␀␀␀␀␀¯Ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀µ⁄0␀␀␀␀␀=€0␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀ûﬁ0␀␀␀␀␀ﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀Aﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀±‚0␀␀␀␀␀GÊ0␀␀␀␀␀ÛÊ0␀␀␀␀␀éÁ0␀␀␀␀␀5Ë0␀␀␀␀␀‚Ë0␀␀␀␀␀ûÈ0␀␀␀␀␀WÍ0␀␀␀␀␀Î0␀␀␀␀␀⁄Î0␀␀␀␀␀ùÏ0␀␀␀␀␀DÌ0␀␀␀␀␀␀Ó0␀␀␀␀␀≤Ó0␀␀␀␀␀›Ó0␀␀␀␀␀›Ô0␀␀␀␀␀ÌÒ0␀␀␀␀␀ÄÚ0␀␀␀␀␀˚Ú0␀␀␀␀␀-ı0␀␀␀␀␀»ı0␀␀␀␀␀yˆ0␀␀␀␀␀˜0␀␀␀␀␀E˜0␀␀␀␀␀¯0␀␀␀␀␀≠¯0␀␀␀␀␀ö˙0␀␀␀␀␀E˚0␀␀␀␀␀¸0␀␀␀␀␀#¸0␀␀␀␀␀"˝0␀␀␀␀␀®˝0␀␀␀␀␀ã˛0␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀ù1␀␀␀␀␀ô1␀␀␀␀␀01␀␀␀␀␀Ô1␀␀␀␀␀h	1␀␀␀␀␀Í	1␀␀␀␀␀9
